epblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Account</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Banking</b>. Under Where we pay you, choose Bank transfer or e-Transfer.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Fill in Account holder, Institution number, Transit number and Account number (or your e-Transfer email).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Submit payout details</b>. For your security we confirm new details by phone before we use them.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/owner/banking</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:990/642"><img src="/guides/img/owner-07-banking-desktop-87b2ffe3.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="990" height="642"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:50.5%;top:25.7%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:90.9%;top:45.5%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:30.3%;top:89.7%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fees-payments-and-payouts-statements-and-payouts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Statements and payouts</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">This month so far, at the top of Statements: the rentals finished this month, your Owner Revenue, the Revenue Share, fees and deductions and the expected payout, worked out live and marked Provisional. Rentals still under way are listed below it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Statements: one a month, once approved by CarmaCars; the approved statement is the final one. Open one to see every booking, the revenue share, deductions and the payout.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Download PDF</b> to keep a copy. We also email it to you with the PDF attached.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Payouts shows what was paid to you and when. Payouts are made on the 10th for the month before.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/owner/statements/380cc1bb-bfd5-4e55-8022-93a3b998ca74</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/792"><img src="/guides/img/owner-09-statement-desktop-fc5f9ea5.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="792"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:16%;top:30.6%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:66%;top:40.9%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Paid a flat monthly payment for a car? Its statement shows a Flat monthly payment line for the month (a part month by the day) instead of the Revenue Share. The car&#39;s rentals are listed without amounts paid to you, as CarmaCars keeps them, and there is no insurance or tracker fee for it. A booking expense is taken off only when we charge it to you; it then shows as an owner cost with its reason. Vehicles shows the amount and since when.</div></aside><h3 class="gd-h3">Fees taken from your statement</h3><p class="gd-p">If you agreed with CarmaCars to have your fees taken from your revenue statement, your invoices are not debited from your bank account. Each invoice is paid from your next owner statement (the line &quot;Invoice INV-..., paid from statement&quot;) and reads <b class="gd-ui">Paid from statement</b>. If a statement does not cover it, the rest is taken from the next one; an invoice still owing 2 months after its billing date is debited from your bank account after the usual notice.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">A flat monthly payment and your agreement</h3><p class="gd-p">If your cars are paid a flat monthly amount, your Enrollment Agreement is the <b class="gd-ui">Flat-Rate Vehicle Enrollment Agreement</b>: a fixed Monthly Amount per car on the payout date, part months by the day, no revenue share and no insurance or tracker fee. When your pay changes from one way to the other, Home shows <b class="gd-ui">Check and sign</b> for the new agreement.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fees-payments-and-payouts-repairs-and-partner-credits" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Repairs and partner credits</h2><p class="gd-p">If CarmaCars turns it on for you, <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Statements</b> also shows the repair costs and partner credits on your own cars this year, with who paid each repair. It is not part of your statements or payouts.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'requests-offers-and-bookings', 'chapter', 'people-and-access', 'A booking starts as a request from the website, or as an offer you send yourself to a customer on the phone. You check it, adjust it and send the offer; an offer that is out is changed in place. After that, the booking page holds the money, documents, changes and history.

## Bookings now: what is out, coming back and owed

Open **Bookings**. It opens on **Now**, one screen that refreshes by itself every 30 seconds. Every time is Toronto time.

1. The numbers at the top: cars out now, due back today, overdue, going out in the next 72 hours, payments due in the next 7 days (with the total) and free cars. Tap one to jump to its list.
2. **Out now**: every car on rent, overdue returns first in red. Each shows the car (photo, code, plate), the renter with **Call** and **Text**, when it was picked up, when it is due back with a countdown, the payment plan and the next payment, the deposit held, and the km and fuel at pickup. Filter by Overdue, Due today or Payment due.
3. A confirmed booking whose pickup time has passed with no check-out recorded is listed as out, with **Out (pickup not recorded)**. The car most likely left. Press **Mark picked up**: it records the pickup at the booked time (change it if the car left at another time), the booking goes on rent, and Fleet gets a task to add the photos, km and fuel. The usual checks stay: the deposit taken (or an Admin waives it with the reason), the renter''s signature (or an Admin''s reason), the agreement''s details, every driver verified and the coverage confirmed. If one is missing, the reason is shown.
4. **Coming back**: overdue, today and tomorrow, by the time each is due.
5. **Going out**: confirmed pickups in the next 72 hours, delivery or pickup, with ticks and crosses for the licence, the signed agreement, the payment, the deposit (a clock until the morning of the pickup day, when the hold is placed on the card on file) and the check-out photos (done at the handover).
6. **Money due**: every rental payment due in the next 7 days or overdue, the amount, the plan and which payment it is (for example 3 of 4).
7. **Free now**: cars available and not out, the longest idle first, with the next pickup; then the cars in maintenance or cleaning. Partners'' cars are counted apart.

> Good to know: Placeholder bookings never show on Now.

### Payment plans

A rental is paid in full at pickup, weekly, every 2 weeks, or monthly. A rental longer than one period (30 days) pays each period by itself. To change it, open the booking, then the **Payment plan** card on Overview or Money, and press **Change the plan**. Each payment is its share of the total by its days, due on the day it starts. An insurer-billed rental shows **Insurer billed** and is never in Money due unless the renter owes a part. Admins, customer service and finance change the plan; fleet sees it.

## All bookings

The **All bookings** tab of Bookings has the search (booking number, name, email, phone, plate or car code), the status (All, Out now, Booked, Returned, Closed, Cancelled) and **Bill to** (All, Renter, Insurer). **Out now** shows the bookings on rent and those whose pickup passed without a check-out, together. Each booking is one row: its number and status in plain words, the car with its photo, the renter with **Call** and **Text**, the dates, the money (paid up, to pay, overdue, insurer billed) and Bill to.

## The request queue

Open **Bookings** > **Requests and offers**. The oldest waiting request is at the top.

1. The numbers at the top: waiting for an offer, past the reply target (red), offers out, accepted but not paid, and offers expired.
2. One queue, the most urgent first: the longest wait, then offers accepted but not paid, then offers out by when they expire. Each row has the car with its photo, the dates, the price, the renter with **Call** and **Text**, the licence (verified, to review, or not uploaded yet), who is answering it, and one button: **Send offer**, **Follow up** or **Open**. **Decline** sits beside **Send offer**.
3. Waiting shows how long the renter has waited ("12 min", "3 h", "2 days"); red means past the first reply target (5 minutes, set in Program settings). **Promise** counts down the 2 hours the site promises the renter.
4. Filter by Active, New, Asked the renter, Changes asked, Offer out, Not paid or Expired. An expired offer leaves the active queue 48 hours after it expired, or once its pickup time passed; Expired lists them all. An offer still out when its pickup time passes expires by itself.

![](/guides/img/admin-02-requests-desktop-6521282d.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 820; address: carmacars.ca/admin/requests; pins: 1 38.9 29.9, 2 22.2 43.3")

> Good to know: A request whose pickup time passes without an offer expires by itself, with a note in its history. The renter is not emailed unless "Email the renter when their request expires that way" is on in Program settings.

## Answer a request with an offer

1. The Review and offer tab shows the request as the renter sent it.
2. Adjust the car, the dates, the rate type, the places, the rates (under **Show rate card**) and fees, the deposit and extras. A place changed away from a delivery or a collection takes its fee box and its fee with it.
3. Price on the right updates as you change things.
4. Add a message, choose how long the offer stays open, then press **Send the offer**.

![](/guides/img/admin-03-booking-review-desktop-353f3707.jpg "desktop; size: 1200 1550; address: carmacars.ca/admin/bookings/CC-10069?tab=review; pins: 1 5.0 6.5, 2 7.5 45.8, 3 74.2 42.6, 4 76.7 98.1")

5. Changed fields but not ready to send? Press **Save changes**. The panel "The offer as the renter sees it" shows the result.
6. Can''t do it? Press **Decline** and fill in Reason and any alternative.
7. Need an answer first? Press **Ask the renter** to send a question.

![](/guides/img/admin-03-booking-review-desktop-4dd4ed06.jpg "desktop; size: 500 80; address: carmacars.ca/admin/bookings/CC-10069?tab=review; pins: 6 41.2 52.5, 7 18.0 52.5")

Opening a request takes it for you: everyone else sees "Being answered by" your name and since when, with Send the offer and Decline off, until you send, decline or leave (20 minutes, renewed while you work; Program settings). Press **Take over** to answer one someone else holds; it is noted in the history. A second answer is refused with who answered and when. A request from the website opens to Sales after 15 minutes (Program settings); until then Admins, customer service and fleet answer it.

## Send an offer without a request

Press **Send an offer** at the top of Bookings, or **Send an offer without a request** on Requests and offers. For a customer on the phone, by text or at the counter: no request needed.

The screen is seven short steps, each with one line saying what to do, and the price beside it (on a phone the total sits at the bottom of the screen: press **See every line**). What most offers never need is under each step''s **More options**, which stays open while something in it is used.

1. **Who is renting and when**: find the renter by name, phone or email, or press **Not on file? Add a new customer** (full legal name, mobile, email for the offer link, date of birth). A customer already on file with the same email or phone is shown with Use: one person, one record. Then the pickup and the return.
2. **Which car**: search by car code, plate or name; each car says Free or Not free for the dates. More options: the rate card and the type and free-only filters.
3. **Where they pick up and return**: at our location, we deliver or collect (the address and distance), an airport or the owner''s location. The fee each one makes shows under it, Automatic or Set by hand.
4. **How damage is covered**: the renter''s own insurance, a credit card or the Protection Plan. More options: another Protection Plan price.
5. **Extras**: add-ons, when the car has any.
6. **The price**: the rate sheet price is filled in. More options: another price (a total for the trip or a rate a day, with why), Amounts I type (before or after HST), the total the renter pays, kilometres, a promo code, the deposit and a discount (an Admin), and **Fees**: press **Change** to set one by hand, **Reset to automatic** to undo it. Below: how it is paid (card online and a card hold unless you change it under More options).
7. **Send it**: who found this client (sales and customer service), a message, and Text or Email. More options: how long the offer is open, the owner''s view, who found the client (an Admin) and the internal note. Above the button, **Ready to send** or **Missing:** with what is left; press Send and each missing field says what it needs. Press **Send the offer to** the renter, or **Save without sending** to keep it as a request for later. **The offer as the renter sees it** is under the price.

> Good to know: Choices drive the charges. Take off a delivery, a collection, the Protection Plan or an add-on and its fee goes with it, even a fee set by hand: there is nothing to remove in a second place. Choose it again and the fee starts from the automatic amount.

> Good to know: It makes the same request and offer the website makes: the renter approves, signs and pays (or you record the payment), and only then is the car on the calendar. No "request received" email goes to the renter for an offer you send. Staff commissions and statements count it like any other booking.

## Change an offer that is out

The renter has the offer (Offered), or approved it and has not paid (Signing and payment). Open **More actions** on the booking and press **Edit the offer**.

1. Change anything: the car, the dates, the places, the price, fees, the deposit, add-ons, how it is paid. Each changed field is highlighted and the before and after are listed. Amounts I type (Before tax or After tax) and the Total the renter pays (after tax) work as on Send an offer.
2. Write what changed in Message to the renter and choose how long the offer is open.
3. Press **Save and send the update**: the renter gets the new version by email or text (ticked), and the old version no longer counts. Or press **Save without telling the renter** and tell them yourself.
4. A confirmed booking is changed with **Change the booking** (Propose a change, below).

> Tip: No need to withdraw first. **Withdraw the offer** is only for taking it back for good; **Send again, later expiry** gives the renter more time, and **Renter approved by phone** records a yes given on a call.

## Edit a booking that has started

On a confirmed, on-trip or returned booking (an Admin: a closed one too), Overview, **Edit the booking**, **Edit**.

1. Change the pickup or the return (extend or shorten: the rental charge is worked out again at this booking''s rates), the car (on trip: the car it leaves goes to Out of service for Fleet to check), the rental charge for the trip, each fee, the kilometres a day, the deposit (an Admin) and the note.
2. Type why, if you like, and tick **Email the renter what changed**, or leave it off for a silent correction. Press **Save the changes**.
3. What is open now shows at once: **Email a pay link** or **Text a pay link** for exactly that amount, **Charge** the saved card (the renter agreed), or record cash or an e-Transfer on the Money tab.

> Good to know: Each edit is kept with who, when, why, before and after (Edits, under the form) and in the booking''s history. A closed booking''s owner split and the staff commission follow. To have the renter accept and sign first, use Propose a change instead.

## Fees, a forgotten fee and the balance

On the booking''s Money tab, Fees lists each fee. Press **Change or add a fee**.

1. Type a new amount (for the whole trip, before HST) beside any fee, or choose one not on the booking (the young driver fee shows its price for these dates), or add a charge of its own with or without HST.
2. Press **Save the fees**. The balance shows by part (rental, fees) with the pay link, the saved card and Record a payment beside it.
3. The renter sees the balance on their booking with a Pay button, and pays by card on Stripe''s form.

> Good to know: Every change is recorded (Changes to the fees): the amount before and after, who and why. Customer service and sales may change fees while Program settings, Staff may change fees, is on.

## A renter with only a debit or prepaid card

A credit card is required by default: the deposit must be on a credit card so the deductible can be charged. The pay page tells a renter with only a debit or prepaid card to contact us.

1. On the booking''s Money tab, press **Allow debit and prepaid cards for this booking** and type the reason. Who and when are kept, and the change is in the booking''s history.
2. The booking''s pay page, staff pay links and deposit hold then take a debit or prepaid card, and the renter is told the hold lowers the money available on the card until it is released, which can take several business days.
3. **Require a credit card again** turns it off.

The Money tab shows each card used and its type (credit, debit, prepaid). A booking on credit card rental coverage is always paid on the credit card that carries the coverage, and cannot be allowed. Program settings, **Card types accepted**, can open debit and prepaid cards to every booking.

## Correct a renter''s details

On the renter''s page (People, Renters) or on any of their bookings, **Edit renter**.

1. Correct the name, email, phone, date of birth, licence, home address (start typing to find it) or the staff note.
2. A new email also becomes their sign-in at once (no confirmation needed for a typo you correct); tick **Email the renter a link to set a password** to send one there. Unsigned agreements and offers go to the new address.
3. Press **Save the renter**. An email that another renter has is refused with their name; the same phone is a warning.
4. The same person entered twice? Possible duplicates (same email, same phone, or same name and date of birth) shows under the renter. **Merge into this record** moves the other record''s bookings, licences, cards, payments, documents and messages here and fills any detail missing here; the other record stays, blocked, with the merge in both histories.

## Payments by part: the rental, the deposit and later charges

On the booking''s Money tab, Money by part shows what is still open for the rental, the fees and later charges, the deposit and the card on file. Each part is paid its own way, in any mix: for example the deposit in cash and the rental by card.

1. **Record a payment**: choose what it is for (the rental, fees, the deposit or a later charge) and how it was paid (e-Transfer, cash, cheque, bank transfer, platform payout, the insurer). An e-Transfer, cheque or transfer needs its reference. Press **Record it**. The renter gets a receipt; **Print** prints one to hand over.
2. **Collect a card**: a payment (Everything open by default: the rental, the fees and any later charge in one), the deposit hold or saving the card. The renter types the card in Stripe''s secure form: on this device (**Open the card form**, then hand it over) or by a link texted or emailed to them (**Send the link**; by text first when the renter has a mobile number). Staff never type a card number.
3. Before every pickup the deposit hold link is texted to the renter on its own: 24 hours before (at once when the pickup is sooner), for a confirmed booking whose deposit is a card hold with no hold yet. The Money tab says **Deposit link texted** and when it was opened; the ready check shows it too. The hold is still needed before the keys. No mobile number, or the text not sent: a task **Deposit link not sent**. **Settings**, then Site settings, Deposit link by text: on or off, and the hours.
4. A deposit hold lasts about 7 days and shows the days left; while the car is out it is collected by itself before it lapses. After the return, settle the deposit (below). **Capture the hold** for all of it keeps the money; a part capture or **Release the hold** waits for the settlement while the car is out or something is open (an Admin may do it with the reason).
5. **Charge the saved card** (Finance or an Admin): extra kilometres, fuel, damage or a late return, with the reason the renter''s receipt shows. For a rental over 7 days, save the card and charge the deposit this way.
6. An offer paid another way: once the renter approved and signed and the money is recorded, the booking is confirmed (or press **Confirm the booking**).
7. A deposit taken in cash or by e-Transfer is given back the same way after the return: Finance gets a task; press **Returned** with the reference or receipt number.

> Good to know: Statements, reconciliation and the deposit settlement read each payment with its method: a cash deposit is never refunded to a card.

## Settle the deposit

The deposit is never given back by itself. Finance or an Admin settles it after the return: on the booking''s Money tab, under Deposit, press **Settle the deposit**. Issue the Check-in statement first.

1. The form shows the deposit, what is still available, the charges owed from the statement and what is taken from the deposit for them. What the deposit does not cover is charged to the card on file; with no card (or a card declined), the renter gets a pay link by email and text, and Finance has a task until it is paid.
2. Tolls and tickets can take up to 7 days to come in. Inside that window the whole rest of the deposit is filled in as the hold-back, until the window ends. To give it back sooner, tick Release now anyway: a toll that comes in later is charged to the card on file.
3. Something still open keeps the whole deposit: an incident, a claim, new damage at the return not priced, damage found later not billed, a toll or ticket on the car during the rental not matched or not charged, a card dispute, or charges not on a statement yet. The form lists them. Only an Admin can release part of it, with the reason; it is recorded.
4. Damage: **Keep the whole deposit (damage)** turns what is left of the deposit into a damage charge, with what was damaged and the photos; the renter is told. **Bill damage** adds a damage charge up to the $2,500 deductible (more goes through a claim): the deposit pays first, then the card on file.
5. Press **Settle**. The money moves at Stripe at once: the charges are collected and what is not owed is refunded or the hold released. A step Stripe refuses is tried again by itself, and Finance gets a task if it keeps failing.

> Good to know: A card hold lapses after about 7 days. While the car is out, or returned and not settled, the hold is collected in full a day and a half before it lapses: that keeps the money, and the settlement refunds what is not owed. A hold that lapses anyway is charged to the saved card, and Finance is told at once.

## A booking

Open **Bookings** > **Bookings**, then a booking number. Or type the number in the search box.

1. Tabs: Overview, Money, Changes, History, and Drivers and documents.
2. Overview shows the trip, the renter, what is still missing for the handover, and the price.
3. Open tasks for this booking, with the queue and the due time.
4. Top right: **Email the renter** and **More actions**, the menu with **Edit the offer**, **Stop blocking the calendar**, **Cancel for the renter**, **Cancel by CarmaCars** and the rest.
5. Under the booking number: **Next step**, what happens next and who does it, with one button for that step (for example **Send the offer**, **Sign on this device** or **Check out the car**); then where the booking is on its way, from Request to Closed, with the dates, the days, the total and who pays.

![](/guides/img/admin-04-booking-desktop-b56b668a.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 960; address: carmacars.ca/admin/bookings/CC-10065; pins: 2 50.0 46.6, 4 85.4 14.5, 5 22.9 26.8")

## Check a car out or in

From the booking, with your phone or a tablet: the same checklist field staff use.

1. A confirmed booking shows **Check out (pickup)** under Check-out, check-in and signing; a booking on rent shows **Check in (return)**. Today lists the check-outs and check-ins due, each with **Check out** or **Check in**.
2. The checklist opens: the ready check, the renter and their licence and card, the odometer (km) and fuel or charge, the keys, the photo set (every side, the wheels, the interior, the odometer and fuel gauge, the plate), damage marks with close-ups, then the renter and you sign.
3. Photos wait on the device without a connection and upload in the background. Each keeps its time, and the place when the device allows location.
4. A field job of the booking is taken over (the history says so); with no job, one is made for you. When done, press **See the photo report**.

> Tip: Fleet, Sales and Customer service check cars out and in the same way from their own booking page.

## The photo report, late returns and the return charges

Under Check-out, check-in and signing, press **Photo report**.

1. The report shows the due-back time, the actual check-out and check-in, Late by (or Overdue by while the car is out), the odometer and kilometres over the allowance, the fuel or charge out and in, every photo with its time and place, and the damage.
2. At check-in the late return (after the grace period of the fee defaults), the mileage overage and the fuel or recharging are written to the return charges at once. A gas car with no pump receipt is priced at the refill price per eighth (Program settings) plus the markup until the receipt is entered.
3. Not charging one? Press **Waive** beside it and give the reason: it stays waived if the charges are worked out again.
4. The time was wrong? Press **Correct the check-in time** (or the check-out time) with the reason: lateness and the late charges follow, and the history keeps both times.
5. The renter gets the same report (without these buttons) by email and in their Documents. Late by shows on the booking and in the Bookings list.

### The renter says the car is back

Every overdue email, text and alert (at the return time, at 15 minutes and the final notice) has a one-tap **I''ve returned the car** link, and the renter''s booking page has the button. The renter can add photos, the odometer, the fuel level and the time they returned it. Sending it stops every overdue notice of the booking at once, the booking shows **Returned, waiting for confirmation**, and Fleet gets an urgent To do: "The renter says the car is back".

1. Open the booking. The card **The renter says the car is back** shows what the renter gave, marked renter-provided, with their photos.
2. Check the car: the return place, the tracker, the photos.
3. Press **Confirm** to complete the trip. Correct the odometer, fuel or return time first if they are wrong: the late charges follow the time you confirm. The renter''s photos join the check-in report.
4. Or press **Deny** and say why. The renter gets your reason by email and text, and the overdue notices start again.

Checking the car in the usual way also completes the trip and stops the notices. Admins, Fleet, Sales, Customer service and field staff can Confirm or Deny.

## Signatures on the spot, or by link

The renter or an additional driver signs the rental agreement on your device, or on their own phone.

1. While a signature is missing, the booking shows **Sign now on this device**, **Email the signing link** and **Text the signing link**.
2. No agreement made yet (the renter has not saved their details at home)? **Sign now on this device** still shows: press **Prepare the agreement to sign now** and it is made on the spot.
3. **Sign now on this device**: confirm the name matches their licence and that you saw the original licence (photograph it if none is on file), then press **Hand the device to** and their name.
4. They read both agreements (CarmaCars'' and Blind Spot''s), tick the statements and sign. Then **Back to the staff view** for the next signer.
5. The record is the same as signing online, and says it was signed in person, collected by you, on your device. It is printed on the signed copy''s signature record page.

## Rental agreements: every version, every field

The booking''s Rental agreements card: the current version of CarmaCars'' and Blind Spot''s agreements, every earlier one, and what is still blank.

1. Once the agreement is signed and countersigned, any change to what it prints makes a new version of both documents by itself: the dates, the price lines, the car, a driver added or corrected, the coverage, the deposit or how it was paid, an address.
2. A change to the dates, the price, the car, the drivers or the coverage option is signed again: the renter (and each driver it affects) gets their link by email and text, and the card shows "Agreement v3 waiting for signature". A correction (a typo in an address, a plate written differently) is filed without signing; the renter gets the corrected copy by email.
3. Check-out makes the "as picked up" copy (time out, km out, fuel out, the car''s plate and VIN, the check-out report), countersigned by whoever checked the car out; check-in makes the closing copy (time in, km in, driven and charged, fuel in, late hours, damage, the return charges, the final totals). Both go to the renter by email.
4. **Every version** lists each one with what changed and both PDFs. **Resend the signing links**, or press the button with their first name beside it to have them sign on your phone or tablet.
5. The card lists what the agreements still print blank (a licence expiry, the insurer''s policy number, the insured vehicle, a VIN). Type the values and press **Save the missing fields**: the agreements follow.
6. Check-out stops while a field a claim needs is blank. An Admin can let it go ahead: type the reason and press **Override**; the reason is in the booking''s history.
7. **Make the agreements again** checks both against the booking at once (they also follow every change by themselves).
8. **Edit the wording** (Admin only) changes CarmaCars'' agreement text for this booking: press **Change** beside a clause, edit its text, say why and press **Save the wording**; **Add** writes Additional terms at the end of Part 2. Only clauses not required by law or the insurer can be removed; the consents are fixed, and Blind Spot''s form (the insurer''s official form) is never changed. Before the renter signs, the agreement is made again; after, the change is a new version they sign, and **Every version** shows each clause before and after.

## Signing that holds up in a dispute

Every signature on the site is made the same way: rental agreements, amendments and new versions (remotely or on your device), and the owner agreements, schedules and forms, a co-owner''s link, the partner, investment and staff agreements.

1. The licence on file is shown. A 6-digit code to their phone or email on file is optional: the signer may press **Verify by code (optional)**, and Program settings, E-signing, **ask for a one-time code** makes it a required first step again (off by default). Without the code, the certificate says the identity was not confirmed by a code.
2. They say they read the documents, initial the key terms (each initials box is saved with **Save initials**; **Clear** takes it back to initial again) (damage and the deductible, the deposit and later charges, fuel, kilometres and late returns, their coverage, cancellation), give three consents (to sign electronically, to receive records electronically, to card charges under the agreement) and draw their signature.
3. Owners, partners, investors and staff do the same for their documents: the code, the reading, the key terms of their documents initialled (for example the Enrollment Agreement''s three confirmations, Form C''s acknowledgments, Schedule C, the staff agreement''s confidentiality), two consents and the drawn signature. Form C''s witness still types their name beside the owner.
4. Each step is recorded with its time, IP address and device, and the place when the device shares it. The signed PDFs end with a certificate of completion; anyone can check a signed file at `carmacars.ca/verify`.
5. Typed names are off. For a signer who cannot draw, an Admin can turn on the accessibility fallback: **Settings** > **Program**, Esign typed fallback.

## Card disputes: the evidence pack

Everything that proves the rental, in one PDF for Stripe.

1. When a card payment is disputed, the evidence pack is built by itself: the signed agreements with their certificates, the check-out and check-in reports with photos, kilometres and fuel, the licence, the payments and charges, every message to the renter, and the card checks from Stripe. It is staged in Stripe as the dispute''s evidence, and To do gets an urgent task.
2. Open the booking: the Rental agreements card shows the pack. Press **Download** to check it, then **Submit to Stripe** before the evidence date.
3. **Build the dispute evidence pack** makes one at any time (an Admin or Finance).

## The licence before an offer is accepted

Front, back and a selfie, from the request on.

1. After sending a request the renter is asked for their licence. A licence already on file from an earlier booking is used again while it is valid after the return.
2. The offer cannot be accepted (by the renter, or by you on their word) and nothing is paid until the licence and its expiry date are on file.
3. Review the images as usual with **Review documents**: the card Renter documents is on Review and offer too.
4. The switch is in **Settings** > **Program**, Booking requests and offers: Booking licence required (on), with the selfie (on).

## Renter documents: licence and proof of coverage

A renter''s licence photos, selfie and proof of coverage (OPCF 27 or a credit card''s rental coverage) are checked before the handover. You check them yourself; no task is needed.

1. A booking with documents waiting is a line on To do: "Check ''s documents for booking ", marked Now when the pickup is within two days. Press **Review documents**.
2. The pop-up shows each driver''s images and the coverage: the insurer, policy number and expiry, or the card, its type and whether the name matches.
3. What to check is written once at the top. One wrong? Open **Reject this one** under it, type the reason the renter reads and press **Reject**: they are asked for a new one.
4. Then press **Approve all**: every image, the proof of coverage and the Protection Plan still waiting are approved in one step. Anything the system refuses is named with the reason.
5. The same pop-up is on the booking: the card Renter documents (**Review documents**) on Overview and on Drivers and documents.

> Tip: Each opening of a renter''s documents is logged. The links to the images last one minute. Field staff can also check a licence in person at the check-out (photos and four checks): the history says "checked in person". Field staff also review the licence images (not the coverage) of bookings on their own jobs in the next 7 days from My jobs, with the same Approve all or a reason to reject: the history says the reviewer''s role, field. Sales review the licence images (not the coverage) of any booking being arranged or under way from their To do or the booking, with the same Approve all or a reason to reject: the history says the role, sales.

## Payments by day

**Money** > **Payments**, the **By day** tab: every payment and refund of a day or a range, by method, the cash drawer and the refunds waiting. Finance has the same screen.

1. Choose From and To and the methods (card, e-Transfer, cash, cheque, platform payout, insurer, bank transfer, pre-authorized debit, other), then press **Show**.
2. Totals by method and for each day; cards read as the card and its last four digits, never a code.
3. The cash drawer: expected (cash in less cash given back) against the count Finance records with **Record the count**; a difference shows over or short.
4. Refunds waiting: every refund asked for anywhere with the policy maths. **Approve** or **Decline** with the reason in the row, then **Issue the refund**.
5. **Export CSV** for the bookkeeper.

## Propose a change to a confirmed booking

The renter gets an email and answers on their booking. The calendar moves only when they accept.

1. Open the booking''s Changes tab. Under Propose a change, set the new pickup, return or car.
2. To price it by hand, type a New rental charge before tax. Leave it empty to use the car''s rates.
3. Write the Reason, for the renter. They read it.
4. Press **Preview the price**, then **Send to the renter**.

![](/guides/img/admin-05-booking-changes-desktop-97008b21.jpg "desktop; size: 1200 520; address: carmacars.ca/admin/bookings/CC-10065?tab=changes; pins: 1 17.5 33.7, 2 9.2 50.0, 3 38.3 71.2, 4 12.9 91.9")

## Who a booking is credited to

Overview (and Review and offer) shows the Sales credit: the staff member the booking counts for in their sales.

1. A quote or a rental is credited to whoever created or added it. A request from the website is credited to whoever sent its first offer.
2. To give it to someone else, press **Reassign**, choose who (or Nobody), say whether they sourced the client and write the reason. The booking''s history and the audit log keep it, and the deal stays in the same week and month.
3. Sourced means the staff member chose I sourced this client when they entered it, it came with a field staff referral link, or you credited it. Only a sourced booking earns a staff commission. A website request earns none unless you credit someone.
4. Someone said they sourced a website request? The credit line shows the claim: press **Credit them** or **Not theirs**, with a reason.
5. A price typed by hand shows beside the rate-sheet price, with the reason. A price under the floor or past the discount limit is flagged: press **Mark reviewed** once you have looked at it.

> Good to know: A request keeps the lead-time adjustment of the moment it came in ("Short-notice pricing +10%" or "Booked ahead −5%"), through the offer and the payment. To change it, open the booking''s review screen, **More options**, **Lead-time pricing (%)**: a number (0 for none), or empty for the tier of the request. A price typed by hand replaces it.

> Tip: The renter has 48 hours to accept (and sign the amendment) or decline, with one reminder. Any extra is charged to their Card on File; a lower price raises a refund for your approval.

## Review requests

Every renter is asked for a review by email and text, as they chose, only from 9 am to 9 pm Toronto time. Nothing needs setting up.

| Message | When |
| --- | --- |
| Mid-trip check-in | Rentals of 2 days or more, 24 hours after the pickup: "How is the car? Reply or call if anything is off." No review ask. |
| Review request | 1 hour after the check-in. It links the review page: the renter taps what they liked, adds a sentence, and gets a short draft to copy and post on Google. |
| Reminder | 24 hours after the request. |
| Final follow-up | 7 days after the request. Nothing more after it. |

1. The booking page has the card Review requests: each message with when it went or when it will go, and why it stopped.
2. **Ask for a review** sends the request now (or at 9 am if it is later than 9 pm), on any booking on a trip, returned or closed. Not twice in 24 hours.
3. On hold: a return or later charge (late return, kilometres, fuel, cleaning, smoking, damage, tolls and tickets) is not settled or waived, or an incident or dispute is open. The request goes by itself once they are. Press **Send anyway** to send it now.
4. **Mark reviewed** stops the messages when the renter tells you they already reviewed.

The messages also stop by themselves when the renter presses "I already left a review", leaves a review on the site, unsubscribes, or a Google review is matched to them. **Bookings** > **Reviews** has the numbers (requests sent, on hold, reviews detected, the average rating), the hold list and the Google reviews to match.

> Tip: The draft is made only from what the renter picked and wrote, and from the booking (the car, how long, delivery or pickup). Everyone gets the Google link, whatever their stars; a renter who gives 3 stars or fewer also sees "Something wasn''t right? Tell us directly".

## What the owner sees, and owner deductions

Each booking on an owner''s or partner''s car shows the card What the owner sees at the top of its page.

1. **Hide from the owner** keeps the booking''s revenue from the owner until the car is returned, or until the owner statement covering it is approved. The owner sees the booking as Booked with its dates, and the calendar still shows the car busy. Add a reason if you like: it is kept in the history.
2. **Show to the owner** shows it now. Approving the statement shows every hidden booking on it by itself.
3. Not shown to the owner is for a booking with no owner revenue (an insurance placeholder, a shareholder''s or the owner''s own use at no charge): the owner sees only that the car is unavailable for those dates. A booking with revenue cannot be set this way.
4. Add a rental and Send an offer have What the owner sees. It starts from Settings > Program, Owners and fleet: Owners see a booking''s revenue (right away by default).
5. On the Money tab, Owner deductions on this booking: **Add a booking expense** (cleaning, repair, fuel, platform fee or other, the amount, the reason the owner reads, a receipt number) comes off before Owner Revenue.
6. **Set the Revenue Share for this booking** applies within the car''s signed terms. Above the terms only an Admin can, with Above the signed terms ticked and the reason. **Back to the car''s terms** undoes it.
7. Add a rental has the same under The car''s owner.

> Good to know: The owner''s statement always includes every booking at its true amounts and lists each deduction with its reason, so the payout is always right. Customer service and sales add deductions only while Program settings let them change fees.

## Email the renter or the adjuster

Press **Email the renter** at the top of a booking, or open its **Messages** tab.

1. Write a **Subject** and a **Message**, or pick a **Quick reply** to start from (Settings > Quick replies keeps them).
2. Press **Email the renter**. It goes from CarmaCars (bookings@carmacars.ca) and replies come back to the bookings inbox. The renter also sees it in their account and can answer there.
3. On a booking an insurer pays, choose **From**: CarmaCars, or Blind Spot Car Rental (insurance). **Email the adjuster** writes to the adjuster''s email on the booking (Insurance claim), always from Blind Spot Car Rental.

The Messages tab shows what you and the renter wrote, newest first, with who wrote it, and every email of the booking with its state (waiting, sent, failed). Each email you send is also in the History tab with your name.

> Good to know: Emails go out through the same daily limit as every email (the line under the form shows today''s use). A message to a renter goes before digests and marketing; past the limit it waits until midnight. To write to a renter from **People** > **Renters**, open the renter: Email the renter is at the bottom, about their latest booking or the one you pick.

### Record the pickup or the return now (details later)
When the car went out or came back but the checklist could not be done (no photos, no time, the renter dropped the keys), the booking''s **Check-out, check-in and signing** card has **Record the pickup now (details later)** on a confirmed booking and **Record the return now (details later)** while the car is on rent. Give the actual time (now, or earlier), the odometer and fuel if you know them, and why. The booking moves on (on rent, or returned), late return charges follow the actual time, and Fleet gets the task **Add the photos and readings for CC-...**. Once returned, the statement can be issued and the deposit settled; releasing the deposit before the photos are in needs an Admin and a reason. A pickup without the deposit taken needs an Admin to waive it with a reason, and without the renter''s signature on the check-out report an Admin''s reason too. Later, **Add the check-out (or check-in) photos and readings** opens the usual checklist (photos, readings, your signature): the task closes when it is saved.

The Agreement card says **Waiting for the renter''s details** when the renter still has blanks to fill (date of birth, address, mobile, licence, coverage): their account asks for them before signing and paying. No email or text is sent.

### Find a booking
**Bookings** has one search box: type the booking number (CC-1042, cc1042 or just 1042), the renter''s or a driver''s name, an email, a phone number in any format, a plate (spaces do not matter) or a car code, then press Enter. The status filters still apply to what is found.

### Record a card payment taken outside the site
A card taken in the Stripe Dashboard, or on a card reader, is recorded on the booking''s **Money** tab with **Record card payment**.

1. Choose what it paid: **Rental and fees**, **Rental**, **Fees**, **Later charges** or **Deposit hold**, and where it was taken.
2. Type the **Last 4 digits** and the amount. A Stripe payment id (pi_... or ch_..., from the payment in the Stripe Dashboard) is optional for a payment: press **Look up** and the amount and last 4 digits are checked against Stripe.
3. Press **Record it**. A payment confirms a booking waiting for payment, as any payment does.

> Good to know: A deposit hold needs its Stripe payment id, so it can be captured or released from **Settle the deposit**. It is recorded as held, with the usual release reminders. A hold on a reader lapses after 2 days, one made online after 7.

### Charge or hold the deposit on the card reader
With the S700 paired (Settings > Card reader), the **Money** tab has **Charge on reader** (everything open, the rental, the fees or a later charge) and **Hold deposit on reader**. Press **Send to the reader**: the amount shows on the reader and the renter taps, inserts or swipes the card. The screen updates by itself; **Cancel** stops the reader and nothing is charged. A deposit hold is captured or released from Settle the deposit like any hold.

### Credit card coverage: the same card
When the renter''s coverage is their credit card, the whole rental (rental and fees) is paid on that same card. The Money tab says which card. Another card on the pay page is refused and refunded at once; on the reader it is refused before the money is taken; a payment by e-Transfer, cash or the like is refused; a card typed by hand needs its last 4 digits and the box **This is the same card**. Deposits and later charges can go on any card. If the renter truly has to use another card or method, press **Allow another card** and give the reason (an Admin).

## Booked as soon as the renter accepts (release 28)

A booking is booked the moment the renter approves the offer. It takes the car on every calendar, the fleet board, the car''s availability and the counts, even before the payment or the pickup is recorded. Payment and the handover show as their own badges: **Booked, payment due** and **Pickup not recorded**. The first renter to approve gets the car: any other open offer on the same car and dates goes back to Requests with a Re-offer To do.

- **Booked, payment due** To do: a booked rental still unpaid within 48 hours of its pickup. Send the pay link, charge the saved card or record the payment.
- Record the pickup To do: a pickup time that passed with nothing recorded, as before.

When you send an offer, **The offer as the renter sees it** sits right under **Send the offer**: check it before you press it.

## Changes after signing: an amended agreement, no new signature

The rental terms (section 15.4) let CarmaCars update a booking after signing: an extension, new dates or times, a price adjustment, a fee, a car swap. The signed agreement keeps applying. Each change makes a new version of the agreement marked **Amended** with the date, carrying the renter''s original signature, and the renter is sent it. Nobody is asked to sign again, except an additional driver who never signed (they sign before driving).

## Check-out and check-in on one screen

On the booking page, **Check out (pickup)** and **Check in (return)** are one screen: the time (now unless you change it), the odometer, the fuel, the photos and a note. Pick many photos at once from the camera roll or take them; tag an angle on any photo if you like. The suggested angles (front, each corner and side, rear, odometer, fuel gauge, interior front and rear, trunk, wheels, any damage) tick themselves as photos are tagged. Nothing is required but the time; the renter''s own photos are added to the same report, each marked with who took it (the renter or staff) and its angle. The full checklist is still one tap away.

## Type into the Blind Spot agreement

On the **Rental agreements** card, **Type into the Blind Spot agreement** shows each box as the form prints it. Change a value and **Save the corrections**: it is drawn in that box, and the insured vehicle, the claim number, the adjuster and missing km or fuel go back onto the booking. **Preview the filled form** opens it with your corrections.

## Reopen an expired offer (release 28)

An expired offer reopens in one click: **Reopen offer** on the booking or on the **Expired** filter of Requests. The renter gets the usual offer email and text; the offer stays open 24 hours unless you type other hours. When the pickup time has passed, the dialog asks for the new pickup and return first. A renter can also press **Ask to reopen this offer**: you get the To do "Renter wants expired offer reopened" and an alert, as for a new request.

An offer sent after its pickup time no longer expires by itself: it expires at its own expiry time (the pickup only counts when the offer was sent before it and the pickup is 2 hours past). The offer screens say **Pickup time has passed: update it** and do not send until you move the pickup.', 'Requests, offers and bookings', 'See what is out, coming back and owed now; send an offer with or without a request, change it in place, take payments by part, run a booking.',
  'A booking starts as a request from the website, or as an offer you send yourself to a customer on the phone. You check it, adjust it and send the offer; an offer that is out is changed in place. After that, the booking page holds the money, documents, changes and history.

## Bookings now: what is out, coming back and owed

Open **Bookings**. It opens on **Now**, one screen that refreshes by itself every 30 seconds. Every time is Toronto time.

1. The numbers at the top: cars out now, due back today, overdue, going out in the next 72 hours, payments due in the next 7 days (with the total) and free cars. Tap one to jump to its list.
2. **Out now**: every car on rent, overdue returns first in red. Each shows the car (photo, code, plate), the renter with **Call** and **Text**, when it was picked up, when it is due back with a countdown, the payment plan and the next payment, the deposit held, and the km and fuel at pickup. Filter by Overdue, Due today or Payment due.
3. A confirmed booking whose pickup time has passed with no check-out recorded is listed as out, with **Out (pickup not recorded)**. The car most likely left. Press **Mark picked up**: it records the pickup at the booked time (change it if the car left at another time), the booking goes on rent, and Fleet gets a task to add the photos, km and fuel. The usual checks stay: the deposit taken (or an Admin waives it with the reason), the renter''s signature (or an Admin''s reason), the agreement''s details, every driver verified and the coverage confirmed. If one is missing, the reason is shown.
4. **Coming back**: overdue, today and tomorrow, by the time each is due.
5. **Going out**: confirmed pickups in the next 72 hours, delivery or pickup, with ticks and crosses for the licence, the signed agreement, the payment, the deposit (a clock until the morning of the pickup day, when the hold is placed on the card on file) and the check-out photos (done at the handover).
6. **Money due**: every rental payment due in the next 7 days or overdue, the amount, the plan and which payment it is (for example 3 of 4).
7. **Free now**: cars available and not out, the longest idle first, with the next pickup; then the cars in maintenance or cleaning. Partners'' cars are counted apart.

> Good to know: Placeholder bookings never show on Now.

### Payment plans

A rental is paid in full at pickup, weekly, every 2 weeks, or monthly. A rental longer than one period (30 days) pays each period by itself. To change it, open the booking, then the **Payment plan** card on Overview or Money, and press **Change the plan**. Each payment is its share of the total by its days, due on the day it starts. An insurer-billed rental shows **Insurer billed** and is never in Money due unless the renter owes a part. Admins, customer service and finance change the plan; fleet sees it.

## All bookings

The **All bookings** tab of Bookings has the search (booking number, name, email, phone, plate or car code), the status (All, Out now, Booked, Returned, Closed, Cancelled) and **Bill to** (All, Renter, Insurer). **Out now** shows the bookings on rent and those whose pickup passed without a check-out, together. Each booking is one row: its number and status in plain words, the car with its photo, the renter with **Call** and **Text**, the dates, the money (paid up, to pay, overdue, insurer billed) and Bill to.

## The request queue

Open **Bookings** > **Requests and offers**. The oldest waiting request is at the top.

1. The numbers at the top: waiting for an offer, past the reply target (red), offers out, accepted but not paid, and offers expired.
2. One queue, the most urgent first: the longest wait, then offers accepted but not paid, then offers out by when they expire. Each row has the car with its photo, the dates, the price, the renter with **Call** and **Text**, the licence (verified, to review, or not uploaded yet), who is answering it, and one button: **Send offer**, **Follow up** or **Open**. **Decline** sits beside **Send offer**.
3. Waiting shows how long the renter has waited ("12 min", "3 h", "2 days"); red means past the first reply target (5 minutes, set in Program settings). **Promise** counts down the 2 hours the site promises the renter.
4. Filter by Active, New, Asked the renter, Changes asked, Offer out, Not paid or Expired. An expired offer leaves the active queue 48 hours after it expired, or once its pickup time passed; Expired lists them all. An offer still out when its pickup time passes expires by itself.

![](/guides/img/admin-02-requests-desktop-6521282d.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 820; address: carmacars.ca/admin/requests; pins: 1 38.9 29.9, 2 22.2 43.3")

> Good to know: A request whose pickup time passes without an offer expires by itself, with a note in its history. The renter is not emailed unless "Email the renter when their request expires that way" is on in Program settings.

## Answer a request with an offer

1. The Review and offer tab shows the request as the renter sent it.
2. Adjust the car, the dates, the rate type, the places, the rates (under **Show rate card**) and fees, the deposit and extras. A place changed away from a delivery or a collection takes its fee box and its fee with it.
3. Price on the right updates as you change things.
4. Add a message, choose how long the offer stays open, then press **Send the offer**.

![](/guides/img/admin-03-booking-review-desktop-353f3707.jpg "desktop; size: 1200 1550; address: carmacars.ca/admin/bookings/CC-10069?tab=review; pins: 1 5.0 6.5, 2 7.5 45.8, 3 74.2 42.6, 4 76.7 98.1")

5. Changed fields but not ready to send? Press **Save changes**. The panel "The offer as the renter sees it" shows the result.
6. Can''t do it? Press **Decline** and fill in Reason and any alternative.
7. Need an answer first? Press **Ask the renter** to send a question.

![](/guides/img/admin-03-booking-review-desktop-4dd4ed06.jpg "desktop; size: 500 80; address: carmacars.ca/admin/bookings/CC-10069?tab=review; pins: 6 41.2 52.5, 7 18.0 52.5")

Opening a request takes it for you: everyone else sees "Being answered by" your name and since when, with Send the offer and Decline off, until you send, decline or leave (20 minutes, renewed while you work; Program settings). Press **Take over** to answer one someone else holds; it is noted in the history. A second answer is refused with who answered and when. A request from the website opens to Sales after 15 minutes (Program settings); until then Admins, customer service and fleet answer it.

## Send an offer without a request

Press **Send an offer** at the top of Bookings, or **Send an offer without a request** on Requests and offers. For a customer on the phone, by text or at the counter: no request needed.

The screen is seven short steps, each with one line saying what to do, and the price beside it (on a phone the total sits at the bottom of the screen: press **See every line**). What most offers never need is under each step''s **More options**, which stays open while something in it is used.

1. **Who is renting and when**: find the renter by name, phone or email, or press **Not on file? Add a new customer** (full legal name, mobile, email for the offer link, date of birth). A customer already on file with the same email or phone is shown with Use: one person, one record. Then the pickup and the return.
2. **Which car**: search by car code, plate or name; each car says Free or Not free for the dates. More options: the rate card and the type and free-only filters.
3. **Where they pick up and return**: at our location, we deliver or collect (the address and distance), an airport or the owner''s location. The fee each one makes shows under it, Automatic or Set by hand.
4. **How damage is covered**: the renter''s own insurance, a credit card or the Protection Plan. More options: another Protection Plan price.
5. **Extras**: add-ons, when the car has any.
6. **The price**: the rate sheet price is filled in. More options: another price (a total for the trip or a rate a day, with why), Amounts I type (before or after HST), the total the renter pays, kilometres, a promo code, the deposit and a discount (an Admin), and **Fees**: press **Change** to set one by hand, **Reset to automatic** to undo it. Below: how it is paid (card online and a card hold unless you change it under More options).
7. **Send it**: who found this client (sales and customer service), a message, and Text or Email. More options: how long the offer is open, the owner''s view, who found the client (an Admin) and the internal note. Above the button, **Ready to send** or **Missing:** with what is left; press Send and each missing field says what it needs. Press **Send the offer to** the renter, or **Save without sending** to keep it as a request for later. **The offer as the renter sees it** is under the price.

> Good to know: Choices drive the charges. Take off a delivery, a collection, the Protection Plan or an add-on and its fee goes with it, even a fee set by hand: there is nothing to remove in a second place. Choose it again and the fee starts from the automatic amount.

> Good to know: It makes the same request and offer the website makes: the renter approves, signs and pays (or you record the payment), and only then is the car on the calendar. No "request received" email goes to the renter for an offer you send. Staff commissions and statements count it like any other booking.

## Change an offer that is out

The renter has the offer (Offered), or approved it and has not paid (Signing and payment). Open **More actions** on the booking and press **Edit the offer**.

1. Change anything: the car, the dates, the places, the price, fees, the deposit, add-ons, how it is paid. Each changed field is highlighted and the before and after are listed. Amounts I type (Before tax or After tax) and the Total the renter pays (after tax) work as on Send an offer.
2. Write what changed in Message to the renter and choose how long the offer is open.
3. Press **Save and send the update**: the renter gets the new version by email or text (ticked), and the old version no longer counts. Or press **Save without telling the renter** and tell them yourself.
4. A confirmed booking is changed with **Change the booking** (Propose a change, below).

> Tip: No need to withdraw first. **Withdraw the offer** is only for taking it back for good; **Send again, later expiry** gives the renter more time, and **Renter approved by phone** records a yes given on a call.

## Edit a booking that has started

On a confirmed, on-trip or returned booking (an Admin: a closed one too), Overview, **Edit the booking**, **Edit**.

1. Change the pickup or the return (extend or shorten: the rental charge is worked out again at this booking''s rates), the car (on trip: the car it leaves goes to Out of service for Fleet to check), the rental charge for the trip, each fee, the kilometres a day, the deposit (an Admin) and the note.
2. Type why, if you like, and tick **Email the renter what changed**, or leave it off for a silent correction. Press **Save the changes**.
3. What is open now shows at once: **Email a pay link** or **Text a pay link** for exactly that amount, **Charge** the saved card (the renter agreed), or record cash or an e-Transfer on the Money tab.

> Good to know: Each edit is kept with who, when, why, before and after (Edits, under the form) and in the booking''s history. A closed booking''s owner split and the staff commission follow. To have the renter accept and sign first, use Propose a change instead.

## Fees, a forgotten fee and the balance

On the booking''s Money tab, Fees lists each fee. Press **Change or add a fee**.

1. Type a new amount (for the whole trip, before HST) beside any fee, or choose one not on the booking (the young driver fee shows its price for these dates), or add a charge of its own with or without HST.
2. Press **Save the fees**. The balance shows by part (rental, fees) with the pay link, the saved card and Record a payment beside it.
3. The renter sees the balance on their booking with a Pay button, and pays by card on Stripe''s form.

> Good to know: Every change is recorded (Changes to the fees): the amount before and after, who and why. Customer service and sales may change fees while Program settings, Staff may change fees, is on.

## A renter with only a debit or prepaid card

A credit card is required by default: the deposit must be on a credit card so the deductible can be charged. The pay page tells a renter with only a debit or prepaid card to contact us.

1. On the booking''s Money tab, press **Allow debit and prepaid cards for this booking** and type the reason. Who and when are kept, and the change is in the booking''s history.
2. The booking''s pay page, staff pay links and deposit hold then take a debit or prepaid card, and the renter is told the hold lowers the money available on the card until it is released, which can take several business days.
3. **Require a credit card again** turns it off.

The Money tab shows each card used and its type (credit, debit, prepaid). A booking on credit card rental coverage is always paid on the credit card that carries the coverage, and cannot be allowed. Program settings, **Card types accepted**, can open debit and prepaid cards to every booking.

## Correct a renter''s details

On the renter''s page (People, Renters) or on any of their bookings, **Edit renter**.

1. Correct the name, email, phone, date of birth, licence, home address (start typing to find it) or the staff note.
2. A new email also becomes their sign-in at once (no confirmation needed for a typo you correct); tick **Email the renter a link to set a password** to send one there. Unsigned agreements and offers go to the new address.
3. Press **Save the renter**. An email that another renter has is refused with their name; the same phone is a warning.
4. The same person entered twice? Possible duplicates (same email, same phone, or same name and date of birth) shows under the renter. **Merge into this record** moves the other record''s bookings, licences, cards, payments, documents and messages here and fills any detail missing here; the other record stays, blocked, with the merge in both histories.

## The Money tab: Rental charges and Security deposit

The booking''s Money tab opens on a strip with the three numbers that matter: **Rental due**, **Deposit** (one word: Not collected, Held, Charged, Released or Partly kept) and **Total paid**. Below are two panels, side by side on a computer and one above the other on a phone. Collecting one never touches the other, and every receipt says which one it is.

**Rental charges**: each line of the price and the total, Paid, then Balance due.

1. The one main button, Collect (the amount) rental: choose how. **The card on file** charges it now (Finance or an Admin); **A payment link by text** or **A payment link by email** sends the renter Stripe''s secure form; **On this device: hand it to the renter** opens it for the renter to type; **Cash, e-Transfer or another way (record it)** records money received (an e-Transfer, cheque or transfer needs its reference). For: the rental and fees together by default, or one of them. The renter gets a receipt; **Print** prints one to hand over.
2. **A later charge**: extra kilometres, fuel, damage or a late return, on the card on file, by a link, on this device, or recorded, with the reason the renter''s receipt shows.
3. **Save a card** saves the renter''s card without charging it. Card readers, the fees (**Change or add a fee**), failed card payments (**Paid another way**), payments received another way and **Refund** sit in this panel too. The history lists rental payments only.
4. An offer paid another way: once the renter approved and signed and the money is recorded, the booking is confirmed (or press **Confirm the booking**).

**Security deposit**: the amount, how it is taken (a credit card hold, a debit or prepaid card at the standard multiple, a charge, or cash), its status in one word and the next step.

1. Not collected: the one main button, Collect (the amount) deposit. **Hold on the card on file** places the hold now (Finance or an Admin); **A deposit hold link by text** or **A deposit hold link by email**, or **A hold on this device: hand it to the renter**; **Charge the card on file as the deposit** only when no hold can be placed; **Cash or e-Transfer (record it)**. The rental balance is not touched.
2. Before every pickup the deposit hold link is texted to the renter on its own: 24 hours before (at once when the pickup is sooner), for a confirmed booking whose deposit is a card hold with no hold yet. The panel says **Deposit link texted** and when it was opened. No mobile number, or the text not sent: a task **Deposit link not sent**. **Settings**, then Site settings, Deposit link by text: on or off, and the hours.
3. Held, while the car is out: **Release** (an Admin, with the reason), **Keep part (damage/fees)** with the amount and the reason, or **Re-authorize the hold** on the saved card before it lapses (the panel shows when the hold expires).
4. After the return: **Settle the deposit** (below).
5. **Waive the deposit** (an Admin, before it is taken), **Change the debit deposit**, and **Allow debit and prepaid cards for this booking** sit in this panel. The history lists deposit payments only.
6. A deposit taken in cash or by e-Transfer is given back the same way after the return: Finance gets a task; press **Returned** with the reference or receipt number.

> Good to know: Statements, reconciliation and the deposit settlement read each payment with its method: a cash deposit is never refunded to a card.

## Settle the deposit

The deposit is never given back by itself. Finance or an Admin settles it after the return: on the booking''s Money tab, under Deposit, press **Settle the deposit**. Issue the Check-in statement first.

1. The form shows the deposit, what is still available, the charges owed from the statement and what is taken from the deposit for them. What the deposit does not cover is charged to the card on file; with no card (or a card declined), the renter gets a pay link by email and text, and Finance has a task until it is paid.
2. Tolls and tickets can take up to 7 days to come in. Inside that window the whole rest of the deposit is filled in as the hold-back, until the window ends. To give it back sooner, tick Release now anyway: a toll that comes in later is charged to the card on file.
3. Something still open keeps the whole deposit: an incident, a claim, new damage at the return not priced, damage found later not billed, a toll or ticket on the car during the rental not matched or not charged, a card dispute, or charges not on a statement yet. The form lists them. Only an Admin can release part of it, with the reason; it is recorded.
4. Damage: **Keep the whole deposit (damage)** turns what is left of the deposit into a damage charge, with what was damaged and the photos; the renter is told. **Bill damage** adds a damage charge up to the $2,500 deductible (more goes through a claim): the deposit pays first, then the card on file.
5. Press **Settle**. The money moves at Stripe at once: the charges are collected and what is not owed is refunded or the hold released. A step Stripe refuses is tried again by itself, and Finance gets a task if it keeps failing.

> Good to know: A card hold lapses after about 7 days. While the car is out, or returned and not settled, the hold is collected in full a day and a half before it lapses: that keeps the money, and the settlement refunds what is not owed. A hold that lapses anyway is charged to the saved card, and Finance is told at once.

## A booking

Open **Bookings** > **Bookings**, then a booking number. Or type the number in the search box.

1. Tabs: Overview, Money, Changes, History, and Drivers and documents.
2. Overview shows the trip, the renter, what is still missing for the handover, and the price.
3. Open tasks for this booking, with the queue and the due time.
4. Top right: **Email the renter** and **More actions**, the menu with **Edit the offer**, **Stop blocking the calendar**, **Cancel for the renter**, **Cancel by CarmaCars** and the rest.
5. Under the booking number: **Next step**, what happens next and who does it, with one button for that step (for example **Send the offer**, **Sign on this device** or **Check out the car**); then where the booking is on its way, from Request to Closed, with the dates, the days, the total and who pays.

![](/guides/img/admin-04-booking-desktop-b56b668a.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 960; address: carmacars.ca/admin/bookings/CC-10065; pins: 2 50.0 46.6, 4 85.4 14.5, 5 22.9 26.8")

## Check a car out or in

From the booking, with your phone or a tablet: the same checklist field staff use.

1. A confirmed booking shows **Check out (pickup)** under Check-out, check-in and signing; a booking on rent shows **Check in (return)**. Today lists the check-outs and check-ins due, each with **Check out** or **Check in**.
2. The checklist opens: the ready check, the renter and their licence and card, the odometer (km) and fuel or charge, the keys, the photo set (every side, the wheels, the interior, the odometer and fuel gauge, the plate), damage marks with close-ups, then the renter and you sign.
3. Photos wait on the device without a connection and upload in the background. Each keeps its time, and the place when the device allows location.
4. A field job of the booking is taken over (the history says so); with no job, one is made for you. When done, press **See the photo report**.

> Tip: Fleet, Sales and Customer service check cars out and in the same way from their own booking page.

## The photo report, late returns and the return charges

Under Check-out, check-in and signing, press **Photo report**.

1. The report shows the due-back time, the actual check-out and check-in, Late by (or Overdue by while the car is out), the odometer and kilometres over the allowance, the fuel or charge out and in, every photo with its time and place, and the damage.
2. At check-in the late return (after the grace period of the fee defaults), the mileage overage and the fuel or recharging are written to the return charges at once. A gas car with no pump receipt is priced at the refill price per eighth (Program settings) plus the markup until the receipt is entered.
3. Not charging one? Press **Waive** beside it and give the reason: it stays waived if the charges are worked out again.
4. The time was wrong? Press **Correct the check-in time** (or the check-out time) with the reason: lateness and the late charges follow, and the history keeps both times.
5. The renter gets the same report (without these buttons) by email and in their Documents. Late by shows on the booking and in the Bookings list.

### The renter says the car is back

Every overdue email, text and alert (at the return time, at 15 minutes and the final notice) has a one-tap **I''ve returned the car** link, and the renter''s booking page has the button. The renter can add photos, the odometer, the fuel level and the time they returned it. Sending it stops every overdue notice of the booking at once, the booking shows **Returned, waiting for confirmation**, and Fleet gets an urgent To do: "The renter says the car is back".

1. Open the booking. The card **The renter says the car is back** shows what the renter gave, marked renter-provided, with their photos.
2. Check the car: the return place, the tracker, the photos.
3. Press **Confirm** to complete the trip. Correct the odometer, fuel or return time first if they are wrong: the late charges follow the time you confirm. The renter''s photos join the check-in report.
4. Or press **Deny** and say why. The renter gets your reason by email and text, and the overdue notices start again.

Checking the car in the usual way also completes the trip and stops the notices. Admins, Fleet, Sales, Customer service and field staff can Confirm or Deny.

## Signatures on the spot, or by link

The renter or an additional driver signs the rental agreement on your device, or on their own phone.

1. While a signature is missing, the booking shows **Sign now on this device**, **Email the signing link** and **Text the signing link**.
2. No agreement made yet (the renter has not saved their details at home)? **Sign now on this device** still shows: press **Prepare the agreement to sign now** and it is made on the spot.
3. **Sign now on this device**: confirm the name matches their licence and that you saw the original licence (photograph it if none is on file), then press **Hand the device to** and their name.
4. They read both agreements (CarmaCars'' and Blind Spot''s), tick the statements and sign. Then **Back to the staff view** for the next signer.
5. The record is the same as signing online, and says it was signed in person, collected by you, on your device. It is printed on the signed copy''s signature record page.

## Rental agreements: every version, every field

The booking''s Rental agreements card: the current version of CarmaCars'' and Blind Spot''s agreements, every earlier one, and what is still blank.

1. Once the agreement is signed and countersigned, any change to what it prints makes a new version of both documents by itself: the dates, the price lines, the car, a driver added or corrected, the coverage, the deposit or how it was paid, an address.
2. A change to the dates, the price, the car, the drivers or the coverage option is signed again: the renter (and each driver it affects) gets their link by email and text, and the card shows "Agreement v3 waiting for signature". A correction (a typo in an address, a plate written differently) is filed without signing; the renter gets the corrected copy by email.
3. Check-out makes the "as picked up" copy (time out, km out, fuel out, the car''s plate and VIN, the check-out report), countersigned by whoever checked the car out; check-in makes the closing copy (time in, km in, driven and charged, fuel in, late hours, damage, the return charges, the final totals). Both go to the renter by email.
4. **Every version** lists each one with what changed and both PDFs. **Resend the signing links**, or press the button with their first name beside it to have them sign on your phone or tablet.
5. The card lists what the agreements still print blank (a licence expiry, the insurer''s policy number, the insured vehicle, a VIN). Type the values and press **Save the missing fields**: the agreements follow.
6. Check-out stops while a field a claim needs is blank. An Admin can let it go ahead: type the reason and press **Override**; the reason is in the booking''s history.
7. **Make the agreements again** checks both against the booking at once (they also follow every change by themselves).
8. **Edit the wording** (Admin only) changes CarmaCars'' agreement text for this booking: press **Change** beside a clause, edit its text, say why and press **Save the wording**; **Add** writes Additional terms at the end of Part 2. Only clauses not required by law or the insurer can be removed; the consents are fixed, and Blind Spot''s form (the insurer''s official form) is never changed. Before the renter signs, the agreement is made again; after, the change is a new version they sign, and **Every version** shows each clause before and after.

## Signing that holds up in a dispute

Every signature on the site is made the same way: rental agreements, amendments and new versions (remotely or on your device), and the owner agreements, schedules and forms, a co-owner''s link, the partner, investment and staff agreements.

1. The licence on file is shown. A 6-digit code to their phone or email on file is optional: the signer may press **Verify by code (optional)**, and Program settings, E-signing, **ask for a one-time code** makes it a required first step again (off by default). Without the code, the certificate says the identity was not confirmed by a code.
2. They say they read the documents, initial the key terms (each initials box is saved with **Save initials**; **Clear** takes it back to initial again) (damage and the deductible, the deposit and later charges, fuel, kilometres and late returns, their coverage, cancellation), give three consents (to sign electronically, to receive records electronically, to card charges under the agreement) and draw their signature.
3. Owners, partners, investors and staff do the same for their documents: the code, the reading, the key terms of their documents initialled (for example the Enrollment Agreement''s three confirmations, Form C''s acknowledgments, Schedule C, the staff agreement''s confidentiality), two consents and the drawn signature. Form C''s witness still types their name beside the owner.
4. Each step is recorded with its time, IP address and device, and the place when the device shares it. The signed PDFs end with a certificate of completion; anyone can check a signed file at `carmacars.ca/verify`.
5. Typed names are off. For a signer who cannot draw, an Admin can turn on the accessibility fallback: **Settings** > **Program**, Esign typed fallback.

## Card disputes: the evidence pack

Everything that proves the rental, in one PDF for Stripe.

1. When a card payment is disputed, the evidence pack is built by itself: the signed agreements with their certificates, the check-out and check-in reports with photos, kilometres and fuel, the licence, the payments and charges, every message to the renter, and the card checks from Stripe. It is staged in Stripe as the dispute''s evidence, and To do gets an urgent task.
2. Open the booking: the Rental agreements card shows the pack. Press **Download** to check it, then **Submit to Stripe** before the evidence date.
3. **Build the dispute evidence pack** makes one at any time (an Admin or Finance).

## The licence before an offer is accepted

Front, back and a selfie, from the request on.

1. After sending a request the renter is asked for their licence. A licence already on file from an earlier booking is used again while it is valid after the return.
2. The offer cannot be accepted (by the renter, or by you on their word) and nothing is paid until the licence and its expiry date are on file.
3. Review the images as usual with **Review documents**: the card Renter documents is on Review and offer too.
4. The switch is in **Settings** > **Program**, Booking requests and offers: Booking licence required (on), with the selfie (on).

## Renter documents: licence and proof of coverage

A renter''s licence photos, selfie and proof of coverage (OPCF 27 or a credit card''s rental coverage) are checked before the handover. You check them yourself; no task is needed.

1. A booking with documents waiting is a line on To do: "Check ''s documents for booking ", marked Now when the pickup is within two days. Press **Review documents**.
2. The pop-up shows each driver''s images and the coverage: the insurer, policy number and expiry, or the card, its type and whether the name matches.
3. What to check is written once at the top. One wrong? Open **Reject this one** under it, type the reason the renter reads and press **Reject**: they are asked for a new one.
4. Then press **Approve all**: every image, the proof of coverage and the Protection Plan still waiting are approved in one step. Anything the system refuses is named with the reason.
5. The same pop-up is on the booking: the card Renter documents (**Review documents**) on Overview and on Drivers and documents.

> Tip: Each opening of a renter''s documents is logged. The links to the images last one minute. Field staff can also check a licence in person at the check-out (photos and four checks): the history says "checked in person". Field staff also review the licence images (not the coverage) of bookings on their own jobs in the next 7 days from My jobs, with the same Approve all or a reason to reject: the history says the reviewer''s role, field. Sales review the licence images (not the coverage) of any booking being arranged or under way from their To do or the booking, with the same Approve all or a reason to reject: the history says the role, sales.

## Payments by day

**Money** > **Payments**, the **By day** tab: every payment and refund of a day or a range, by method, the cash drawer and the refunds waiting. Finance has the same screen.

1. Choose From and To and the methods (card, e-Transfer, cash, cheque, platform payout, insurer, bank transfer, pre-authorized debit, other), then press **Show**.
2. Totals by method and for each day; cards read as the card and its last four digits, never a code.
3. The cash drawer: expected (cash in less cash given back) against the count Finance records with **Record the count**; a difference shows over or short.
4. Refunds waiting: every refund asked for anywhere with the policy maths. **Approve** or **Decline** with the reason in the row, then **Issue the refund**.
5. **Export CSV** for the bookkeeper.

## Propose a change to a confirmed booking

The renter gets an email and answers on their booking. The calendar moves only when they accept.

1. Open the booking''s Changes tab. Under Propose a change, set the new pickup, return or car.
2. To price it by hand, type a New rental charge before tax. Leave it empty to use the car''s rates.
3. Write the Reason, for the renter. They read it.
4. Press **Preview the price**, then **Send to the renter**.

![](/guides/img/admin-05-booking-changes-desktop-97008b21.jpg "desktop; size: 1200 520; address: carmacars.ca/admin/bookings/CC-10065?tab=changes; pins: 1 17.5 33.7, 2 9.2 50.0, 3 38.3 71.2, 4 12.9 91.9")

## Who a booking is credited to

Overview (and Review and offer) shows the Sales credit: the staff member the booking counts for in their sales.

1. A quote or a rental is credited to whoever created or added it. A request from the website is credited to whoever sent its first offer.
2. To give it to someone else, press **Reassign**, choose who (or Nobody), say whether they sourced the client and write the reason. The booking''s history and the audit log keep it, and the deal stays in the same week and month.
3. Sourced means the staff member chose I sourced this client when they entered it, it came with a field staff referral link, or you credited it. Only a sourced booking earns a staff commission. A website request earns none unless you credit someone.
4. Someone said they sourced a website request? The credit line shows the claim: press **Credit them** or **Not theirs**, with a reason.
5. A price typed by hand shows beside the rate-sheet price, with the reason. A price under the floor or past the discount limit is flagged: press **Mark reviewed** once you have looked at it.

> Good to know: A request keeps the lead-time adjustment of the moment it came in ("Short-notice pricing +10%" or "Booked ahead −5%"), through the offer and the payment. To change it, open the booking''s review screen, **More options**, **Lead-time pricing (%)**: a number (0 for none), or empty for the tier of the request. A price typed by hand replaces it.

> Tip: The renter has 48 hours to accept (and sign the amendment) or decline, with one reminder. Any extra is charged to their Card on File; a lower price raises a refund for your approval.

## Review requests

Every renter is asked for a review by email and text, as they chose, only from 9 am to 9 pm Toronto time. Nothing needs setting up.

| Message | When |
| --- | --- |
| Mid-trip check-in | Rentals of 2 days or more, 24 hours after the pickup: "How is the car? Reply or call if anything is off." No review ask. |
| Review request | 1 hour after the check-in. It links the review page: the renter taps what they liked, adds a sentence, and gets a short draft to copy and post on Google. |
| Reminder | 24 hours after the request. |
| Final follow-up | 7 days after the request. Nothing more after it. |

1. The booking page has the card Review requests: each message with when it went or when it will go, and why it stopped.
2. **Ask for a review** sends the request now (or at 9 am if it is later than 9 pm), on any booking on a trip, returned or closed. Not twice in 24 hours.
3. On hold: a return or later charge (late return, kilometres, fuel, cleaning, smoking, damage, tolls and tickets) is not settled or waived, or an incident or dispute is open. The request goes by itself once they are. Press **Send anyway** to send it now.
4. **Mark reviewed** stops the messages when the renter tells you they already reviewed.

The messages also stop by themselves when the renter presses "I already left a review", leaves a review on the site, unsubscribes, or a Google review is matched to them. **Bookings** > **Reviews** has the numbers (requests sent, on hold, reviews detected, the average rating), the hold list and the Google reviews to match.

> Tip: The draft is made only from what the renter picked and wrote, and from the booking (the car, how long, delivery or pickup). Everyone gets the Google link, whatever their stars; a renter who gives 3 stars or fewer also sees "Something wasn''t right? Tell us directly".

## What the owner sees, and owner deductions

Each booking on an owner''s or partner''s car shows the card What the owner sees at the top of its page.

1. **Hide from the owner** keeps the booking''s revenue from the owner until the car is returned, or until the owner statement covering it is approved. The owner sees the booking as Booked with its dates, and the calendar still shows the car busy. Add a reason if you like: it is kept in the history.
2. **Show to the owner** shows it now. Approving the statement shows every hidden booking on it by itself.
3. Not shown to the owner is for a booking with no owner revenue (an insurance placeholder, a shareholder''s or the owner''s own use at no charge): the owner sees only that the car is unavailable for those dates. A booking with revenue cannot be set this way.
4. Add a rental and Send an offer have What the owner sees. It starts from Settings > Program, Owners and fleet: Owners see a booking''s revenue (right away by default).
5. On the Money tab, Owner deductions on this booking: **Add a booking expense** (cleaning, repair, fuel, platform fee or other, the amount, the reason the owner reads, a receipt number) comes off before Owner Revenue.
6. **Set the Revenue Share for this booking** applies within the car''s signed terms. Above the terms only an Admin can, with Above the signed terms ticked and the reason. **Back to the car''s terms** undoes it.
7. Add a rental has the same under The car''s owner.

> Good to know: The owner''s statement always includes every booking at its true amounts and lists each deduction with its reason, so the payout is always right. Customer service and sales add deductions only while Program settings let them change fees.

## Email the renter or the adjuster

Press **Email the renter** at the top of a booking, or open its **Messages** tab.

1. Write a **Subject** and a **Message**, or pick a **Quick reply** to start from (Settings > Quick replies keeps them).
2. Press **Email the renter**. It goes from CarmaCars (bookings@carmacars.ca) and replies come back to the bookings inbox. The renter also sees it in their account and can answer there.
3. On a booking an insurer pays, choose **From**: CarmaCars, or Blind Spot Car Rental (insurance). **Email the adjuster** writes to the adjuster''s email on the booking (Insurance claim), always from Blind Spot Car Rental.

The Messages tab shows what you and the renter wrote, newest first, with who wrote it, and every email of the booking with its state (waiting, sent, failed). Each email you send is also in the History tab with your name.

> Good to know: Emails go out through the same daily limit as every email (the line under the form shows today''s use). A message to a renter goes before digests and marketing; past the limit it waits until midnight. To write to a renter from **People** > **Renters**, open the renter: Email the renter is at the bottom, about their latest booking or the one you pick.

### Record the pickup or the return now (details later)
When the car went out or came back but the checklist could not be done (no photos, no time, the renter dropped the keys), the booking''s **Check-out, check-in and signing** card has **Record the pickup now (details later)** on a confirmed booking and **Record the return now (details later)** while the car is on rent. Give the actual time (now, or earlier), the odometer and fuel if you know them, and why. The booking moves on (on rent, or returned), late return charges follow the actual time, and Fleet gets the task **Add the photos and readings for CC-...**. Once returned, the statement can be issued and the deposit settled; releasing the deposit before the photos are in needs an Admin and a reason. A pickup without the deposit taken needs an Admin to waive it with a reason, and without the renter''s signature on the check-out report an Admin''s reason too. Later, **Add the check-out (or check-in) photos and readings** opens the usual checklist (photos, readings, your signature): the task closes when it is saved.

The Agreement card says **Waiting for the renter''s details** when the renter still has blanks to fill (date of birth, address, mobile, licence, coverage): their account asks for them before signing and paying. No email or text is sent.

### Find a booking
**Bookings** has one search box: type the booking number (CC-1042, cc1042 or just 1042), the renter''s or a driver''s name, an email, a phone number in any format, a plate (spaces do not matter) or a car code, then press Enter. The status filters still apply to what is found.

### Record a card payment taken outside the site
A card taken in the Stripe Dashboard, or on a card reader, is recorded on the booking''s **Money** tab with **Record card payment**.

1. Choose what it paid: **Rental and fees**, **Rental**, **Fees**, **Later charges** or **Deposit hold**, and where it was taken.
2. Type the **Last 4 digits** and the amount. A Stripe payment id (pi_... or ch_..., from the payment in the Stripe Dashboard) is optional for a payment: press **Look up** and the amount and last 4 digits are checked against Stripe.
3. Press **Record it**. A payment confirms a booking waiting for payment, as any payment does.

> Good to know: A deposit hold needs its Stripe payment id, so it can be captured or released from **Settle the deposit**. It is recorded as held, with the usual release reminders. A hold on a reader lapses after 2 days, one made online after 7.

### Charge or hold the deposit on the card reader
With the S700 paired (Settings > Card reader), the **Money** tab has **Charge on reader** (everything open, the rental, the fees or a later charge) and **Hold deposit on reader**. Press **Send to the reader**: the amount shows on the reader and the renter taps, inserts or swipes the card. The screen updates by itself; **Cancel** stops the reader and nothing is charged. A deposit hold is captured or released from Settle the deposit like any hold.

### Credit card coverage: the same card
When the renter''s coverage is their credit card, the whole rental (rental and fees) is paid on that same card. The Money tab says which card. Another card on the pay page is refused and refunded at once; on the reader it is refused before the money is taken; a payment by e-Transfer, cash or the like is refused; a card typed by hand needs its last 4 digits and the box **This is the same card**. Deposits and later charges can go on any card. If the renter truly has to use another card or method, press **Allow another card** and give the reason (an Admin).

## Booked as soon as the renter accepts (release 28)

A booking is booked the moment the renter approves the offer. It takes the car on every calendar, the fleet board, the car''s availability and the counts, even before the payment or the pickup is recorded. Payment and the handover show as their own badges: **Booked, payment due** and **Pickup not recorded**. The first renter to approve gets the car: any other open offer on the same car and dates goes back to Requests with a Re-offer To do.

- **Booked, payment due** To do: a booked rental still unpaid within 48 hours of its pickup. Send the pay link, charge the saved card or record the payment.
- Record the pickup To do: a pickup time that passed with nothing recorded, as before.

When you send an offer, **The offer as the renter sees it** sits right under **Send the offer**: check it before you press it.

## Changes after signing: an amended agreement, no new signature

The rental terms (section 15.4) let CarmaCars update a booking after signing: an extension, new dates or times, a price adjustment, a fee, a car swap. The signed agreement keeps applying. Each change makes a new version of the agreement marked **Amended** with the date, carrying the renter''s original signature, and the renter is sent it. Nobody is asked to sign again, except an additional driver who never signed (they sign before driving).

## Check-out and check-in on one screen

On the booking page, **Check out (pickup)** and **Check in (return)** are one screen: the time (now unless you change it), the odometer, the fuel, the photos and a note. Pick many photos at once from the camera roll or take them; tag an angle on any photo if you like. The suggested angles (front, each corner and side, rear, odometer, fuel gauge, interior front and rear, trunk, wheels, any damage) tick themselves as photos are tagged. Nothing is required but the time; the renter''s own photos are added to the same report, each marked with who took it (the renter or staff) and its angle. The full checklist is still one tap away.

## Type into the Blind Spot agreement

On the **Rental agreements** card, **Type into the Blind Spot agreement** shows each box as the form prints it. Change a value and **Save the corrections**: it is drawn in that box, and the insured vehicle, the claim number, the adjuster and missing km or fuel go back onto the booking. **Preview the filled form** opens it with your corrections.

## Reopen an expired offer (release 28)

An expired offer reopens in one click: **Reopen offer** on the booking or on the **Expired** filter of Requests. The renter gets the usual offer email and text; the offer stays open 24 hours unless you type other hours. When the pickup time has passed, the dialog asks for the new pickup and return first. A renter can also press **Ask to reopen this offer**: you get the To do "Renter wants expired offer reopened" and an alert, as for a new request.

An offer sent after its pickup time no longer expires by itself: it expires at its own expiry time (the pickup only counts when the offer was sent before it and the pickup is 2 hours past). The offer screens say **Pickup time has passed: update it** and do not send until you move the pickup.',
  '<p class="gd-p">A booking starts as a request from the website, or as an offer you send yourself to a customer on the phone. You check it, adjust it and send the offer; an offer that is out is changed in place. After that, the booking page holds the money, documents, changes and history.</p><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-bookings-now-what-is-out-coming-back-and-owed" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Bookings now: what is out, coming back and owed</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b>. It opens on <b class="gd-ui">Now</b>, one screen that refreshes by itself every 30 seconds. Every time is Toronto time.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The numbers at the top: cars out now, due back today, overdue, going out in the next 72 hours, payments due in the next 7 days (with the total) and free cars. Tap one to jump to its list.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Out now</b>: every car on rent, overdue returns first in red. Each shows the car (photo, code, plate), the renter with <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b>, when it was picked up, when it is due back with a countdown, the payment plan and the next payment, the deposit held, and the km and fuel at pickup. Filter by Overdue, Due today or Payment due.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A confirmed booking whose pickup time has passed with no check-out recorded is listed as out, with <b class="gd-ui">Out (pickup not recorded)</b>. The car most likely left. Press <b class="gd-ui">Mark picked up</b>: it records the pickup at the booked time (change it if the car left at another time), the booking goes on rent, and Fleet gets a task to add the photos, km and fuel. The usual checks stay: the deposit taken (or an Admin waives it with the reason), the renter&#39;s signature (or an Admin&#39;s reason), the agreement&#39;s details, every driver verified and the coverage confirmed. If one is missing, the reason is shown.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Coming back</b>: overdue, today and tomorrow, by the time each is due.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Going out</b>: confirmed pickups in the next 72 hours, delivery or pickup, with ticks and crosses for the licence, the signed agreement, the payment, the deposit (a clock until the morning of the pickup day, when the hold is placed on the card on file) and the check-out photos (done at the handover).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Money due</b>: every rental payment due in the next 7 days or overdue, the amount, the plan and which payment it is (for example 3 of 4).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Free now</b>: cars available and not out, the longest idle first, with the next pickup; then the cars in maintenance or cleaning. Partners&#39; cars are counted apart.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Placeholder bookings never show on Now.</div></aside><h3 class="gd-h3">Payment plans</h3><p class="gd-p">A rental is paid in full at pickup, weekly, every 2 weeks, or monthly. A rental longer than one period (30 days) pays each period by itself. To change it, open the booking, then the <b class="gd-ui">Payment plan</b> card on Overview or Money, and press <b class="gd-ui">Change the plan</b>. Each payment is its share of the total by its days, due on the day it starts. An insurer-billed rental shows <b class="gd-ui">Insurer billed</b> and is never in Money due unless the renter owes a part. Admins, customer service and finance change the plan; fleet sees it.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-all-bookings" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">All bookings</h2><p class="gd-p">The <b class="gd-ui">All bookings</b> tab of Bookings has the search (booking number, name, email, phone, plate or car code), the status (All, Out now, Booked, Returned, Closed, Cancelled) and <b class="gd-ui">Bill to</b> (All, Renter, Insurer). <b class="gd-ui">Out now</b> shows the bookings on rent and those whose pickup passed without a check-out, together. Each booking is one row: its number and status in plain words, the car with its photo, the renter with <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b>, the dates, the money (paid up, to pay, overdue, insurer billed) and Bill to.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-the-request-queue" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The request queue</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Requests and offers</b>. The oldest waiting request is at the top.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The numbers at the top: waiting for an offer, past the reply target (red), offers out, accepted but not paid, and offers expired.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">One queue, the most urgent first: the longest wait, then offers accepted but not paid, then offers out by when they expire. Each row has the car with its photo, the dates, the price, the renter with <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b>, the licence (verified, to review, or not uploaded yet), who is answering it, and one button: <b class="gd-ui">Send offer</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Follow up</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Open</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b> sits beside <b class="gd-ui">Send offer</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Waiting shows how long the renter has waited (&quot;12 min&quot;, &quot;3 h&quot;, &quot;2 days&quot;); red means past the first reply target (5 minutes, set in Program settings). <b class="gd-ui">Promise</b> counts down the 2 hours the site promises the renter.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Filter by Active, New, Asked the renter, Changes asked, Offer out, Not paid or Expired. An expired offer leaves the active queue 48 hours after it expired, or once its pickup time passed; Expired lists them all. An offer still out when its pickup time passes expires by itself.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/requests</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/820"><img src="/guides/img/admin-02-requests-desktop-6521282d.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="820"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:38.9%;top:29.9%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:22.2%;top:43.3%" aria-hidden="true">2</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A request whose pickup time passes without an offer expires by itself, with a note in its history. The renter is not emailed unless &quot;Email the renter when their request expires that way&quot; is on in Program settings.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-answer-a-request-with-an-offer" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Answer a request with an offer</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The Review and offer tab shows the request as the renter sent it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Adjust the car, the dates, the rate type, the places, the rates (under <b class="gd-ui">Show rate card</b>) and fees, the deposit and extras. A place changed away from a delivery or a collection takes its fee box and its fee with it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Price on the right updates as you change things.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Add a message, choose how long the offer stays open, then press <b class="gd-ui">Send the offer</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/bookings/CC-10069?tab=review</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1200/1550"><img src="/guides/img/admin-03-booking-review-desktop-353f3707.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1200" height="1550"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:5%;top:6.5%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:7.5%;top:45.8%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:74.2%;top:42.6%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:76.7%;top:98.1%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol" start="5"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Changed fields but not ready to send? Press <b class="gd-ui">Save changes</b>. The panel &quot;The offer as the renter sees it&quot; shows the result.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Can&#39;t do it? Press <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b> and fill in Reason and any alternative.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Need an answer first? Press <b class="gd-ui">Ask the renter</b> to send a question.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/bookings/CC-10069?tab=review</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:500/80"><img src="/guides/img/admin-03-booking-review-desktop-4dd4ed06.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="500" height="80"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:41.2%;top:52.5%" aria-hidden="true">6</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:18%;top:52.5%" aria-hidden="true">7</span></div></div></figure></div><p class="gd-p">Opening a request takes it for you: everyone else sees &quot;Being answered by&quot; your name and since when, with Send the offer and Decline off, until you send, decline or leave (20 minutes, renewed while you work; Program settings). Press <b class="gd-ui">Take over</b> to answer one someone else holds; it is noted in the history. A second answer is refused with who answered and when. A request from the website opens to Sales after 15 minutes (Program settings); until then Admins, customer service and fleet answer it.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-send-an-offer-without-a-request" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Send an offer without a request</h2><p class="gd-p">Press <b class="gd-ui">Send an offer</b> at the top of Bookings, or <b class="gd-ui">Send an offer without a request</b> on Requests and offers. For a customer on the phone, by text or at the counter: no request needed.</p><p class="gd-p">The screen is seven short steps, each with one line saying what to do, and the price beside it (on a phone the total sits at the bottom of the screen: press <b class="gd-ui">See every line</b>). What most offers never need is under each step&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">More options</b>, which stays open while something in it is used.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Who is renting and when</b>: find the renter by name, phone or email, or press <b class="gd-ui">Not on file? Add a new customer</b> (full legal name, mobile, email for the offer link, date of birth). A customer already on file with the same email or phone is shown with Use: one person, one record. Then the pickup and the return.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Which car</b>: search by car code, plate or name; each car says Free or Not free for the dates. More options: the rate card and the type and free-only filters.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Where they pick up and return</b>: at our location, we deliver or collect (the address and distance), an airport or the owner&#39;s location. The fee each one makes shows under it, Automatic or Set by hand.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">How damage is covered</b>: the renter&#39;s own insurance, a credit card or the Protection Plan. More options: another Protection Plan price.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Extras</b>: add-ons, when the car has any.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">The price</b>: the rate sheet price is filled in. More options: another price (a total for the trip or a rate a day, with why), Amounts I type (before or after HST), the total the renter pays, kilometres, a promo code, the deposit and a discount (an Admin), and <b class="gd-ui">Fees</b>: press <b class="gd-ui">Change</b> to set one by hand, <b class="gd-ui">Reset to automatic</b> to undo it. Below: how it is paid (card online and a card hold unless you change it under More options).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Send it</b>: who found this client (sales and customer service), a message, and Text or Email. More options: how long the offer is open, the owner&#39;s view, who found the client (an Admin) and the internal note. Above the button, <b class="gd-ui">Ready to send</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Missing:</b> with what is left; press Send and each missing field says what it needs. Press <b class="gd-ui">Send the offer to</b> the renter, or <b class="gd-ui">Save without sending</b> to keep it as a request for later. <b class="gd-ui">The offer as the renter sees it</b> is under the price.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Choices drive the charges. Take off a delivery, a collection, the Protection Plan or an add-on and its fee goes with it, even a fee set by hand: there is nothing to remove in a second place. Choose it again and the fee starts from the automatic amount.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>It makes the same request and offer the website makes: the renter approves, signs and pays (or you record the payment), and only then is the car on the calendar. No &quot;request received&quot; email goes to the renter for an offer you send. Staff commissions and statements count it like any other booking.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-change-an-offer-that-is-out" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Change an offer that is out</h2><p class="gd-p">The renter has the offer (Offered), or approved it and has not paid (Signing and payment). Open <b class="gd-ui">More actions</b> on the booking and press <b class="gd-ui">Edit the offer</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Change anything: the car, the dates, the places, the price, fees, the deposit, add-ons, how it is paid. Each changed field is highlighted and the before and after are listed. Amounts I type (Before tax or After tax) and the Total the renter pays (after tax) work as on Send an offer.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Write what changed in Message to the renter and choose how long the offer is open.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save and send the update</b>: the renter gets the new version by email or text (ticked), and the old version no longer counts. Or press <b class="gd-ui">Save without telling the renter</b> and tell them yourself.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A confirmed booking is changed with <b class="gd-ui">Change the booking</b> (Propose a change, below).</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>No need to withdraw first. <b class="gd-ui">Withdraw the offer</b> is only for taking it back for good; <b class="gd-ui">Send again, later expiry</b> gives the renter more time, and <b class="gd-ui">Renter approved by phone</b> records a yes given on a call.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-edit-a-booking-that-has-started" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Edit a booking that has started</h2><p class="gd-p">On a confirmed, on-trip or returned booking (an Admin: a closed one too), Overview, <b class="gd-ui">Edit the booking</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Edit</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Change the pickup or the return (extend or shorten: the rental charge is worked out again at this booking&#39;s rates), the car (on trip: the car it leaves goes to Out of service for Fleet to check), the rental charge for the trip, each fee, the kilometres a day, the deposit (an Admin) and the note.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Type why, if you like, and tick <b class="gd-ui">Email the renter what changed</b>, or leave it off for a silent correction. Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the changes</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">What is open now shows at once: <b class="gd-ui">Email a pay link</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Text a pay link</b> for exactly that amount, <b class="gd-ui">Charge</b> the saved card (the renter agreed), or record cash or an e-Transfer on the Money tab.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Each edit is kept with who, when, why, before and after (Edits, under the form) and in the booking&#39;s history. A closed booking&#39;s owner split and the staff commission follow. To have the renter accept and sign first, use Propose a change instead.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-fees-a-forgotten-fee-and-the-balance" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Fees, a forgotten fee and the balance</h2><p class="gd-p">On the booking&#39;s Money tab, Fees lists each fee. Press <b class="gd-ui">Change or add a fee</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Type a new amount (for the whole trip, before HST) beside any fee, or choose one not on the booking (the young driver fee shows its price for these dates), or add a charge of its own with or without HST.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the fees</b>. The balance shows by part (rental, fees) with the pay link, the saved card and Record a payment beside it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The renter sees the balance on their booking with a Pay button, and pays by card on Stripe&#39;s form.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Every change is recorded (Changes to the fees): the amount before and after, who and why. Customer service and sales may change fees while Program settings, Staff may change fees, is on.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-a-renter-with-only-a-debit-or-prepaid-card" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A renter with only a debit or prepaid card</h2><p class="gd-p">A credit card is required by default: the deposit must be on a credit card so the deductible can be charged. The pay page tells a renter with only a debit or prepaid card to contact us.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On the booking&#39;s Money tab, press <b class="gd-ui">Allow debit and prepaid cards for this booking</b> and type the reason. Who and when are kept, and the change is in the booking&#39;s history.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The booking&#39;s pay page, staff pay links and deposit hold then take a debit or prepaid card, and the renter is told the hold lowers the money available on the card until it is released, which can take several business days.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Require a credit card again</b> turns it off.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">The Money tab shows each card used and its type (credit, debit, prepaid). A booking on credit card rental coverage is always paid on the credit card that carries the coverage, and cannot be allowed. Program settings, <b class="gd-ui">Card types accepted</b>, can open debit and prepaid cards to every booking.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-correct-a-renter-s-details" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Correct a renter&#39;s details</h2><p class="gd-p">On the renter&#39;s page (People, Renters) or on any of their bookings, <b class="gd-ui">Edit renter</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Correct the name, email, phone, date of birth, licence, home address (start typing to find it) or the staff note.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A new email also becomes their sign-in at once (no confirmation needed for a typo you correct); tick <b class="gd-ui">Email the renter a link to set a password</b> to send one there. Unsigned agreements and offers go to the new address.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the renter</b>. An email that another renter has is refused with their name; the same phone is a warning.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The same person entered twice? Possible duplicates (same email, same phone, or same name and date of birth) shows under the renter. <b class="gd-ui">Merge into this record</b> moves the other record&#39;s bookings, licences, cards, payments, documents and messages here and fills any detail missing here; the other record stays, blocked, with the merge in both histories.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-the-money-tab-rental-charges-and-security-deposit" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The Money tab: Rental charges and Security deposit</h2><p class="gd-p">The booking&#39;s Money tab opens on a strip with the three numbers that matter: <b class="gd-ui">Rental due</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Deposit</b> (one word: Not collected, Held, Charged, Released or Partly kept) and <b class="gd-ui">Total paid</b>. Below are two panels, side by side on a computer and one above the other on a phone. Collecting one never touches the other, and every receipt says which one it is.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Rental charges</b>: each line of the price and the total, Paid, then Balance due.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The one main button, Collect (the amount) rental: choose how. <b class="gd-ui">The card on file</b> charges it now (Finance or an Admin); <b class="gd-ui">A payment link by text</b> or <b class="gd-ui">A payment link by email</b> sends the renter Stripe&#39;s secure form; <b class="gd-ui">On this device: hand it to the renter</b> opens it for the renter to type; <b class="gd-ui">Cash, e-Transfer or another way (record it)</b> records money received (an e-Transfer, cheque or transfer needs its reference). For: the rental and fees together by default, or one of them. The renter gets a receipt; <b class="gd-ui">Print</b> prints one to hand over.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">A later charge</b>: extra kilometres, fuel, damage or a late return, on the card on file, by a link, on this device, or recorded, with the reason the renter&#39;s receipt shows.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Save a card</b> saves the renter&#39;s card without charging it. Card readers, the fees (<b class="gd-ui">Change or add a fee</b>), failed card payments (<b class="gd-ui">Paid another way</b>), payments received another way and <b class="gd-ui">Refund</b> sit in this panel too. The history lists rental payments only.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">An offer paid another way: once the renter approved and signed and the money is recorded, the booking is confirmed (or press <b class="gd-ui">Confirm the booking</b>).</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Security deposit</b>: the amount, how it is taken (a credit card hold, a debit or prepaid card at the standard multiple, a charge, or cash), its status in one word and the next step.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Not collected: the one main button, Collect (the amount) deposit. <b class="gd-ui">Hold on the card on file</b> places the hold now (Finance or an Admin); <b class="gd-ui">A deposit hold link by text</b> or <b class="gd-ui">A deposit hold link by email</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">A hold on this device: hand it to the renter</b>; <b class="gd-ui">Charge the card on file as the deposit</b> only when no hold can be placed; <b class="gd-ui">Cash or e-Transfer (record it)</b>. The rental balance is not touched.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Before every pickup the deposit hold link is texted to the renter on its own: 24 hours before (at once when the pickup is sooner), for a confirmed booking whose deposit is a card hold with no hold yet. The panel says <b class="gd-ui">Deposit link texted</b> and when it was opened. No mobile number, or the text not sent: a task <b class="gd-ui">Deposit link not sent</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, then Site settings, Deposit link by text: on or off, and the hours.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Held, while the car is out: <b class="gd-ui">Release</b> (an Admin, with the reason), <b class="gd-ui">Keep part (damage/fees)</b> with the amount and the reason, or <b class="gd-ui">Re-authorize the hold</b> on the saved card before it lapses (the panel shows when the hold expires).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">After the return: <b class="gd-ui">Settle the deposit</b> (below).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Waive the deposit</b> (an Admin, before it is taken), <b class="gd-ui">Change the debit deposit</b>, and <b class="gd-ui">Allow debit and prepaid cards for this booking</b> sit in this panel. The history lists deposit payments only.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">A deposit taken in cash or by e-Transfer is given back the same way after the return: Finance gets a task; press <b class="gd-ui">Returned</b> with the reference or receipt number.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Statements, reconciliation and the deposit settlement read each payment with its method: a cash deposit is never refunded to a card.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-settle-the-deposit" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Settle the deposit</h2><p class="gd-p">The deposit is never given back by itself. Finance or an Admin settles it after the return: on the booking&#39;s Money tab, under Deposit, press <b class="gd-ui">Settle the deposit</b>. Issue the Check-in statement first.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The form shows the deposit, what is still available, the charges owed from the statement and what is taken from the deposit for them. What the deposit does not cover is charged to the card on file; with no card (or a card declined), the renter gets a pay link by email and text, and Finance has a task until it is paid.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Tolls and tickets can take up to 7 days to come in. Inside that window the whole rest of the deposit is filled in as the hold-back, until the window ends. To give it back sooner, tick Release now anyway: a toll that comes in later is charged to the card on file.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Something still open keeps the whole deposit: an incident, a claim, new damage at the return not priced, damage found later not billed, a toll or ticket on the car during the rental not matched or not charged, a card dispute, or charges not on a statement yet. The form lists them. Only an Admin can release part of it, with the reason; it is recorded.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Damage: <b class="gd-ui">Keep the whole deposit (damage)</b> turns what is left of the deposit into a damage charge, with what was damaged and the photos; the renter is told. <b class="gd-ui">Bill damage</b> adds a damage charge up to the $2,500 deductible (more goes through a claim): the deposit pays first, then the card on file.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Settle</b>. The money moves at Stripe at once: the charges are collected and what is not owed is refunded or the hold released. A step Stripe refuses is tried again by itself, and Finance gets a task if it keeps failing.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A card hold lapses after about 7 days. While the car is out, or returned and not settled, the hold is collected in full a day and a half before it lapses: that keeps the money, and the settlement refunds what is not owed. A hold that lapses anyway is charged to the saved card, and Finance is told at once.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-a-booking" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A booking</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b>, then a booking number. Or type the number in the search box.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Tabs: Overview, Money, Changes, History, and Drivers and documents.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Overview shows the trip, the renter, what is still missing for the handover, and the price.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Open tasks for this booking, with the queue and the due time.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Top right: <b class="gd-ui">Email the renter</b> and <b class="gd-ui">More actions</b>, the menu with <b class="gd-ui">Edit the offer</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Stop blocking the calendar</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Cancel for the renter</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Cancel by CarmaCars</b> and the rest.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Under the booking number: <b class="gd-ui">Next step</b>, what happens next and who does it, with one button for that step (for example <b class="gd-ui">Send the offer</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Sign on this device</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Check out the car</b>); then where the booking is on its way, from Request to Closed, with the dates, the days, the total and who pays.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/bookings/CC-10065</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/960"><img src="/guides/img/admin-04-booking-desktop-b56b668a.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="960"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:50%;top:46.6%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:85.4%;top:14.5%" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:22.9%;top:26.8%" aria-hidden="true">5</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-check-a-car-out-or-in" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Check a car out or in</h2><p class="gd-p">From the booking, with your phone or a tablet: the same checklist field staff use.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A confirmed booking shows <b class="gd-ui">Check out (pickup)</b> under Check-out, check-in and signing; a booking on rent shows <b class="gd-ui">Check in (return)</b>. Today lists the check-outs and check-ins due, each with <b class="gd-ui">Check out</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Check in</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The checklist opens: the ready check, the renter and their licence and card, the odometer (km) and fuel or charge, the keys, the photo set (every side, the wheels, the interior, the odometer and fuel gauge, the plate), damage marks with close-ups, then the renter and you sign.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Photos wait on the device without a connection and upload in the background. Each keeps its time, and the place when the device allows location.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A field job of the booking is taken over (the history says so); with no job, one is made for you. When done, press <b class="gd-ui">See the photo report</b>.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Fleet, Sales and Customer service check cars out and in the same way from their own booking page.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-the-photo-report-late-returns-and-the-return-charges" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The photo report, late returns and the return charges</h2><p class="gd-p">Under Check-out, check-in and signing, press <b class="gd-ui">Photo report</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The report shows the due-back time, the actual check-out and check-in, Late by (or Overdue by while the car is out), the odometer and kilometres over the allowance, the fuel or charge out and in, every photo with its time and place, and the damage.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">At check-in the late return (after the grace period of the fee defaults), the mileage overage and the fuel or recharging are written to the return charges at once. A gas car with no pump receipt is priced at the refill price per eighth (Program settings) plus the markup until the receipt is entered.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Not charging one? Press <b class="gd-ui">Waive</b> beside it and give the reason: it stays waived if the charges are worked out again.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The time was wrong? Press <b class="gd-ui">Correct the check-in time</b> (or the check-out time) with the reason: lateness and the late charges follow, and the history keeps both times.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The renter gets the same report (without these buttons) by email and in their Documents. Late by shows on the booking and in the Bookings list.</div></li></ol></div><h3 class="gd-h3">The renter says the car is back</h3><p class="gd-p">Every overdue email, text and alert (at the return time, at 15 minutes and the final notice) has a one-tap <b class="gd-ui">I&#39;ve returned the car</b> link, and the renter&#39;s booking page has the button. The renter can add photos, the odometer, the fuel level and the time they returned it. Sending it stops every overdue notice of the booking at once, the booking shows <b class="gd-ui">Returned, waiting for confirmation</b>, and Fleet gets an urgent To do: &quot;The renter says the car is back&quot;.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the booking. The card <b class="gd-ui">The renter says the car is back</b> shows what the renter gave, marked renter-provided, with their photos.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Check the car: the return place, the tracker, the photos.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Confirm</b> to complete the trip. Correct the odometer, fuel or return time first if they are wrong: the late charges follow the time you confirm. The renter&#39;s photos join the check-in report.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Or press <b class="gd-ui">Deny</b> and say why. The renter gets your reason by email and text, and the overdue notices start again.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Checking the car in the usual way also completes the trip and stops the notices. Admins, Fleet, Sales, Customer service and field staff can Confirm or Deny.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-signatures-on-the-spot-or-by-link" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Signatures on the spot, or by link</h2><p class="gd-p">The renter or an additional driver signs the rental agreement on your device, or on their own phone.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">While a signature is missing, the booking shows <b class="gd-ui">Sign now on this device</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Email the signing link</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Text the signing link</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">No agreement made yet (the renter has not saved their details at home)? <b class="gd-ui">Sign now on this device</b> still shows: press <b class="gd-ui">Prepare the agreement to sign now</b> and it is made on the spot.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Sign now on this device</b>: confirm the name matches their licence and that you saw the original licence (photograph it if none is on file), then press <b class="gd-ui">Hand the device to</b> and their name.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">They read both agreements (CarmaCars&#39; and Blind Spot&#39;s), tick the statements and sign. Then <b class="gd-ui">Back to the staff view</b> for the next signer.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The record is the same as signing online, and says it was signed in person, collected by you, on your device. It is printed on the signed copy&#39;s signature record page.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-rental-agreements-every-version-every-field" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Rental agreements: every version, every field</h2><p class="gd-p">The booking&#39;s Rental agreements card: the current version of CarmaCars&#39; and Blind Spot&#39;s agreements, every earlier one, and what is still blank.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Once the agreement is signed and countersigned, any change to what it prints makes a new version of both documents by itself: the dates, the price lines, the car, a driver added or corrected, the coverage, the deposit or how it was paid, an address.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A change to the dates, the price, the car, the drivers or the coverage option is signed again: the renter (and each driver it affects) gets their link by email and text, and the card shows &quot;Agreement v3 waiting for signature&quot;. A correction (a typo in an address, a plate written differently) is filed without signing; the renter gets the corrected copy by email.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Check-out makes the &quot;as picked up&quot; copy (time out, km out, fuel out, the car&#39;s plate and VIN, the check-out report), countersigned by whoever checked the car out; check-in makes the closing copy (time in, km in, driven and charged, fuel in, late hours, damage, the return charges, the final totals). Both go to the renter by email.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Every version</b> lists each one with what changed and both PDFs. <b class="gd-ui">Resend the signing links</b>, or press the button with their first name beside it to have them sign on your phone or tablet.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The card lists what the agreements still print blank (a licence expiry, the insurer&#39;s policy number, the insured vehicle, a VIN). Type the values and press <b class="gd-ui">Save the missing fields</b>: the agreements follow.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Check-out stops while a field a claim needs is blank. An Admin can let it go ahead: type the reason and press <b class="gd-ui">Override</b>; the reason is in the booking&#39;s history.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Make the agreements again</b> checks both against the booking at once (they also follow every change by themselves).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Edit the wording</b> (Admin only) changes CarmaCars&#39; agreement text for this booking: press <b class="gd-ui">Change</b> beside a clause, edit its text, say why and press <b class="gd-ui">Save the wording</b>; <b class="gd-ui">Add</b> writes Additional terms at the end of Part 2. Only clauses not required by law or the insurer can be removed; the consents are fixed, and Blind Spot&#39;s form (the insurer&#39;s official form) is never changed. Before the renter signs, the agreement is made again; after, the change is a new version they sign, and <b class="gd-ui">Every version</b> shows each clause before and after.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-signing-that-holds-up-in-a-dispute" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Signing that holds up in a dispute</h2><p class="gd-p">Every signature on the site is made the same way: rental agreements, amendments and new versions (remotely or on your device), and the owner agreements, schedules and forms, a co-owner&#39;s link, the partner, investment and staff agreements.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The licence on file is shown. A 6-digit code to their phone or email on file is optional: the signer may press <b class="gd-ui">Verify by code (optional)</b>, and Program settings, E-signing, <b class="gd-ui">ask for a one-time code</b> makes it a required first step again (off by default). Without the code, the certificate says the identity was not confirmed by a code.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">They say they read the documents, initial the key terms (each initials box is saved with <b class="gd-ui">Save initials</b>; <b class="gd-ui">Clear</b> takes it back to initial again) (damage and the deductible, the deposit and later charges, fuel, kilometres and late returns, their coverage, cancellation), give three consents (to sign electronically, to receive records electronically, to card charges under the agreement) and draw their signature.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Owners, partners, investors and staff do the same for their documents: the code, the reading, the key terms of their documents initialled (for example the Enrollment Agreement&#39;s three confirmations, Form C&#39;s acknowledgments, Schedule C, the staff agreement&#39;s confidentiality), two consents and the drawn signature. Form C&#39;s witness still types their name beside the owner.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Each step is recorded with its time, IP address and device, and the place when the device shares it. The signed PDFs end with a certificate of completion; anyone can check a signed file at <span class="gd-url">carmacars.ca/verify</span>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Typed names are off. For a signer who cannot draw, an Admin can turn on the accessibility fallback: <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>, Esign typed fallback.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-card-disputes-the-evidence-pack" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Card disputes: the evidence pack</h2><p class="gd-p">Everything that proves the rental, in one PDF for Stripe.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">When a card payment is disputed, the evidence pack is built by itself: the signed agreements with their certificates, the check-out and check-in reports with photos, kilometres and fuel, the licence, the payments and charges, every message to the renter, and the card checks from Stripe. It is staged in Stripe as the dispute&#39;s evidence, and To do gets an urgent task.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open the booking: the Rental agreements card shows the pack. Press <b class="gd-ui">Download</b> to check it, then <b class="gd-ui">Submit to Stripe</b> before the evidence date.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Build the dispute evidence pack</b> makes one at any time (an Admin or Finance).</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-the-licence-before-an-offer-is-accepted" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The licence before an offer is accepted</h2><p class="gd-p">Front, back and a selfie, from the request on.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">After sending a request the renter is asked for their licence. A licence already on file from an earlier booking is used again while it is valid after the return.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The offer cannot be accepted (by the renter, or by you on their word) and nothing is paid until the licence and its expiry date are on file.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Review the images as usual with <b class="gd-ui">Review documents</b>: the card Renter documents is on Review and offer too.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The switch is in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>, Booking requests and offers: Booking licence required (on), with the selfie (on).</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-renter-documents-licence-and-proof-of-coverage" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Renter documents: licence and proof of coverage</h2><p class="gd-p">A renter&#39;s licence photos, selfie and proof of coverage (OPCF 27 or a credit card&#39;s rental coverage) are checked before the handover. You check them yourself; no task is needed.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A booking with documents waiting is a line on To do: &quot;Check &#39;s documents for booking &quot;, marked Now when the pickup is within two days. Press <b class="gd-ui">Review documents</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The pop-up shows each driver&#39;s images and the coverage: the insurer, policy number and expiry, or the card, its type and whether the name matches.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">What to check is written once at the top. One wrong? Open <b class="gd-ui">Reject this one</b> under it, type the reason the renter reads and press <b class="gd-ui">Reject</b>: they are asked for a new one.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Then press <b class="gd-ui">Approve all</b>: every image, the proof of coverage and the Protection Plan still waiting are approved in one step. Anything the system refuses is named with the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The same pop-up is on the booking: the card Renter documents (<b class="gd-ui">Review documents</b>) on Overview and on Drivers and documents.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Each opening of a renter&#39;s documents is logged. The links to the images last one minute. Field staff can also check a licence in person at the check-out (photos and four checks): the history says &quot;checked in person&quot;. Field staff also review the licence images (not the coverage) of bookings on their own jobs in the next 7 days from My jobs, with the same Approve all or a reason to reject: the history says the reviewer&#39;s role, field. Sales review the licence images (not the coverage) of any booking being arranged or under way from their To do or the booking, with the same Approve all or a reason to reject: the history says the role, sales.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-payments-by-day" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Payments by day</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Payments</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">By day</b> tab: every payment and refund of a day or a range, by method, the cash drawer and the refunds waiting. Finance has the same screen.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Choose From and To and the methods (card, e-Transfer, cash, cheque, platform payout, insurer, bank transfer, pre-authorized debit, other), then press <b class="gd-ui">Show</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Totals by method and for each day; cards read as the card and its last four digits, never a code.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The cash drawer: expected (cash in less cash given back) against the count Finance records with <b class="gd-ui">Record the count</b>; a difference shows over or short.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Refunds waiting: every refund asked for anywhere with the policy maths. <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b> with the reason in the row, then <b class="gd-ui">Issue the refund</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Export CSV</b> for the bookkeeper.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-propose-a-change-to-a-confirmed-booking" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Propose a change to a confirmed booking</h2><p class="gd-p">The renter gets an email and answers on their booking. The calendar moves only when they accept.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the booking&#39;s Changes tab. Under Propose a change, set the new pickup, return or car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">To price it by hand, type a New rental charge before tax. Leave it empty to use the car&#39;s rates.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Write the Reason, for the renter. They read it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Preview the price</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Send to the renter</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/bookings/CC-10065?tab=changes</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1200/520"><img src="/guides/img/admin-05-booking-changes-desktop-97008b21.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1200" height="520"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:17.5%;top:33.7%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:9.2%;top:50%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:38.3%;top:71.2%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:12.9%;top:91.9%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-who-a-booking-is-credited-to" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Who a booking is credited to</h2><p class="gd-p">Overview (and Review and offer) shows the Sales credit: the staff member the booking counts for in their sales.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A quote or a rental is credited to whoever created or added it. A request from the website is credited to whoever sent its first offer.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">To give it to someone else, press <b class="gd-ui">Reassign</b>, choose who (or Nobody), say whether they sourced the client and write the reason. The booking&#39;s history and the audit log keep it, and the deal stays in the same week and month.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Sourced means the staff member chose I sourced this client when they entered it, it came with a field staff referral link, or you credited it. Only a sourced booking earns a staff commission. A website request earns none unless you credit someone.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Someone said they sourced a website request? The credit line shows the claim: press <b class="gd-ui">Credit them</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Not theirs</b>, with a reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">A price typed by hand shows beside the rate-sheet price, with the reason. A price under the floor or past the discount limit is flagged: press <b class="gd-ui">Mark reviewed</b> once you have looked at it.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A request keeps the lead-time adjustment of the moment it came in (&quot;Short-notice pricing +10%&quot; or &quot;Booked ahead −5%&quot;), through the offer and the payment. To change it, open the booking&#39;s review screen, <b class="gd-ui">More options</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Lead-time pricing (%)</b>: a number (0 for none), or empty for the tier of the request. A price typed by hand replaces it.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The renter has 48 hours to accept (and sign the amendment) or decline, with one reminder. Any extra is charged to their Card on File; a lower price raises a refund for your approval.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-review-requests" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Review requests</h2><p class="gd-p">Every renter is asked for a review by email and text, as they chose, only from 9 am to 9 pm Toronto time. Nothing needs setting up.</p><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Message</th><th scope="col">When</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Mid-trip check-in</td><td>Rentals of 2 days or more, 24 hours after the pickup: &quot;How is the car? Reply or call if anything is off.&quot; No review ask.</td></tr><tr><td>Review request</td><td>1 hour after the check-in. It links the review page: the renter taps what they liked, adds a sentence, and gets a short draft to copy and post on Google.</td></tr><tr><td>Reminder</td><td>24 hours after the request.</td></tr><tr><td>Final follow-up</td><td>7 days after the request. Nothing more after it.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The booking page has the card Review requests: each message with when it went or when it will go, and why it stopped.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Ask for a review</b> sends the request now (or at 9 am if it is later than 9 pm), on any booking on a trip, returned or closed. Not twice in 24 hours.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">On hold: a return or later charge (late return, kilometres, fuel, cleaning, smoking, damage, tolls and tickets) is not settled or waived, or an incident or dispute is open. The request goes by itself once they are. Press <b class="gd-ui">Send anyway</b> to send it now.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Mark reviewed</b> stops the messages when the renter tells you they already reviewed.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">The messages also stop by themselves when the renter presses &quot;I already left a review&quot;, leaves a review on the site, unsubscribes, or a Google review is matched to them. <b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Reviews</b> has the numbers (requests sent, on hold, reviews detected, the average rating), the hold list and the Google reviews to match.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The draft is made only from what the renter picked and wrote, and from the booking (the car, how long, delivery or pickup). Everyone gets the Google link, whatever their stars; a renter who gives 3 stars or fewer also sees &quot;Something wasn&#39;t right? Tell us directly&quot;.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-what-the-owner-sees-and-owner-deductions" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">What the owner sees, and owner deductions</h2><p class="gd-p">Each booking on an owner&#39;s or partner&#39;s car shows the card What the owner sees at the top of its page.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Hide from the owner</b> keeps the booking&#39;s revenue from the owner until the car is returned, or until the owner statement covering it is approved. The owner sees the booking as Booked with its dates, and the calendar still shows the car busy. Add a reason if you like: it is kept in the history.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Show to the owner</b> shows it now. Approving the statement shows every hidden booking on it by itself.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Not shown to the owner is for a booking with no owner revenue (an insurance placeholder, a shareholder&#39;s or the owner&#39;s own use at no charge): the owner sees only that the car is unavailable for those dates. A booking with revenue cannot be set this way.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Add a rental and Send an offer have What the owner sees. It starts from Settings &gt; Program, Owners and fleet: Owners see a booking&#39;s revenue (right away by default).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">On the Money tab, Owner deductions on this booking: <b class="gd-ui">Add a booking expense</b> (cleaning, repair, fuel, platform fee or other, the amount, the reason the owner reads, a receipt number) comes off before Owner Revenue.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Set the Revenue Share for this booking</b> applies within the car&#39;s signed terms. Above the terms only an Admin can, with Above the signed terms ticked and the reason. <b class="gd-ui">Back to the car&#39;s terms</b> undoes it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Add a rental has the same under The car&#39;s owner.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The owner&#39;s statement always includes every booking at its true amounts and lists each deduction with its reason, so the payout is always right. Customer service and sales add deductions only while Program settings let them change fees.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-email-the-renter-or-the-adjuster" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Email the renter or the adjuster</h2><p class="gd-p">Press <b class="gd-ui">Email the renter</b> at the top of a booking, or open its <b class="gd-ui">Messages</b> tab.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Write a <b class="gd-ui">Subject</b> and a <b class="gd-ui">Message</b>, or pick a <b class="gd-ui">Quick reply</b> to start from (Settings &gt; Quick replies keeps them).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Email the renter</b>. It goes from CarmaCars (bookings@carmacars.ca) and replies come back to the bookings inbox. The renter also sees it in their account and can answer there.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">On a booking an insurer pays, choose <b class="gd-ui">From</b>: CarmaCars, or Blind Spot Car Rental (insurance). <b class="gd-ui">Email the adjuster</b> writes to the adjuster&#39;s email on the booking (Insurance claim), always from Blind Spot Car Rental.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">The Messages tab shows what you and the renter wrote, newest first, with who wrote it, and every email of the booking with its state (waiting, sent, failed). Each email you send is also in the History tab with your name.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Emails go out through the same daily limit as every email (the line under the form shows today&#39;s use). A message to a renter goes before digests and marketing; past the limit it waits until midnight. To write to a renter from <b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Renters</b>, open the renter: Email the renter is at the bottom, about their latest booking or the one you pick.</div></aside><h3 class="gd-h3">Record the pickup or the return now (details later)</h3><p class="gd-p">When the car went out or came back but the checklist could not be done (no photos, no time, the renter dropped the keys), the booking&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Check-out, check-in and signing</b> card has <b class="gd-ui">Record the pickup now (details later)</b> on a confirmed booking and <b class="gd-ui">Record the return now (details later)</b> while the car is on rent. Give the actual time (now, or earlier), the odometer and fuel if you know them, and why. The booking moves on (on rent, or returned), late return charges follow the actual time, and Fleet gets the task <b class="gd-ui">Add the photos and readings for CC-...</b>. Once returned, the statement can be issued and the deposit settled; releasing the deposit before the photos are in needs an Admin and a reason. A pickup without the deposit taken needs an Admin to waive it with a reason, and without the renter&#39;s signature on the check-out report an Admin&#39;s reason too. Later, <b class="gd-ui">Add the check-out (or check-in) photos and readings</b> opens the usual checklist (photos, readings, your signature): the task closes when it is saved.</p><p class="gd-p">The Agreement card says <b class="gd-ui">Waiting for the renter&#39;s details</b> when the renter still has blanks to fill (date of birth, address, mobile, licence, coverage): their account asks for them before signing and paying. No email or text is sent.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">Find a booking</h3><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b> has one search box: type the booking number (CC-1042, cc1042 or just 1042), the renter&#39;s or a driver&#39;s name, an email, a phone number in any format, a plate (spaces do not matter) or a car code, then press Enter. The status filters still apply to what is found.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">Record a card payment taken outside the site</h3><p class="gd-p">A card taken in the Stripe Dashboard, or on a card reader, is recorded on the booking&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> tab with <b class="gd-ui">Record card payment</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Choose what it paid: <b class="gd-ui">Rental and fees</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Rental</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Fees</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Later charges</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Deposit hold</b>, and where it was taken.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Type the <b class="gd-ui">Last 4 digits</b> and the amount. A Stripe payment id (pi_... or ch_..., from the payment in the Stripe Dashboard) is optional for a payment: press <b class="gd-ui">Look up</b> and the amount and last 4 digits are checked against Stripe.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Record it</b>. A payment confirms a booking waiting for payment, as any payment does.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A deposit hold needs its Stripe payment id, so it can be captured or released from <b class="gd-ui">Settle the deposit</b>. It is recorded as held, with the usual release reminders. A hold on a reader lapses after 2 days, one made online after 7.</div></aside><h3 class="gd-h3">Charge or hold the deposit on the card reader</h3><p class="gd-p">With the S700 paired (Settings &gt; Card reader), the <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> tab has <b class="gd-ui">Charge on reader</b> (everything open, the rental, the fees or a later charge) and <b class="gd-ui">Hold deposit on reader</b>. Press <b class="gd-ui">Send to the reader</b>: the amount shows on the reader and the renter taps, inserts or swipes the card. The screen updates by itself; <b class="gd-ui">Cancel</b> stops the reader and nothing is charged. A deposit hold is captured or released from Settle the deposit like any hold.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">Credit card coverage: the same card</h3><p class="gd-p">When the renter&#39;s coverage is their credit card, the whole rental (rental and fees) is paid on that same card. The Money tab says which card. Another card on the pay page is refused and refunded at once; on the reader it is refused before the money is taken; a payment by e-Transfer, cash or the like is refused; a card typed by hand needs its last 4 digits and the box <b class="gd-ui">This is the same card</b>. Deposits and later charges can go on any card. If the renter truly has to use another card or method, press <b class="gd-ui">Allow another card</b> and give the reason (an Admin).</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-booked-as-soon-as-the-renter-accepts-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Booked as soon as the renter accepts (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p">A booking is booked the moment the renter approves the offer. It takes the car on every calendar, the fleet board, the car&#39;s availability and the counts, even before the payment or the pickup is recorded. Payment and the handover show as their own badges: <b class="gd-ui">Booked, payment due</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Pickup not recorded</b>. The first renter to approve gets the car: any other open offer on the same car and dates goes back to Requests with a Re-offer To do.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Booked, payment due</b> To do: a booked rental still unpaid within 48 hours of its pickup. Send the pay link, charge the saved card or record the payment.</li><li>Record the pickup To do: a pickup time that passed with nothing recorded, as before.</li></ul><p class="gd-p">When you send an offer, <b class="gd-ui">The offer as the renter sees it</b> sits right under <b class="gd-ui">Send the offer</b>: check it before you press it.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-changes-after-signing-an-amended-agreement-no-new-signature" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Changes after signing: an amended agreement, no new signature</h2><p class="gd-p">The rental terms (section 15.4) let CarmaCars update a booking after signing: an extension, new dates or times, a price adjustment, a fee, a car swap. The signed agreement keeps applying. Each change makes a new version of the agreement marked <b class="gd-ui">Amended</b> with the date, carrying the renter&#39;s original signature, and the renter is sent it. Nobody is asked to sign again, except an additional driver who never signed (they sign before driving).</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-check-out-and-check-in-on-one-screen" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Check-out and check-in on one screen</h2><p class="gd-p">On the booking page, <b class="gd-ui">Check out (pickup)</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Check in (return)</b> are one screen: the time (now unless you change it), the odometer, the fuel, the photos and a note. Pick many photos at once from the camera roll or take them; tag an angle on any photo if you like. The suggested angles (front, each corner and side, rear, odometer, fuel gauge, interior front and rear, trunk, wheels, any damage) tick themselves as photos are tagged. Nothing is required but the time; the renter&#39;s own photos are added to the same report, each marked with who took it (the renter or staff) and its angle. The full checklist is still one tap away.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-type-into-the-blind-spot-agreement" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Type into the Blind Spot agreement</h2><p class="gd-p">On the <b class="gd-ui">Rental agreements</b> card, <b class="gd-ui">Type into the Blind Spot agreement</b> shows each box as the form prints it. Change a value and <b class="gd-ui">Save the corrections</b>: it is drawn in that box, and the insured vehicle, the claim number, the adjuster and missing km or fuel go back onto the booking. <b class="gd-ui">Preview the filled form</b> opens it with your corrections.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-reopen-an-expired-offer-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Reopen an expired offer (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p">An expired offer reopens in one click: <b class="gd-ui">Reopen offer</b> on the booking or on the <b class="gd-ui">Expired</b> filter of Requests. The renter gets the usual offer email and text; the offer stays open 24 hours unless you type other hours. When the pickup time has passed, the dialog asks for the new pickup and return first. A renter can also press <b class="gd-ui">Ask to reopen this offer</b>: you get the To do &quot;Renter wants expired offer reopened&quot; and an alert, as for a new request.</p><p class="gd-p">An offer sent after its pickup time no longer expires by itself: it expires at its own expiry time (the pickup only counts when the offer was sent before it and the pickup is 2 hours past). The offer screens say <b class="gd-ui">Pickup time has passed: update it</b> and do not send until you move the pickup.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'owner-money', 'chapter', 'owners-and-onboarding', 'Owner fee invoices are issued on the notice day and debited on the 15th. Invoices of any amount are made by hand, as drafts first. Statements are built, approved and issued each month, and payouts follow.

## Owner invoices

**Money** > **Owner money**, the **Invoices** tab. Every owner invoice, drafts and voids included. The same list is on each owner''s and each application''s Invoices tab.

1. Filter by Drafts, Open, Partly paid, Paid, Failed, In arrears or Void, or search by invoice number or owner. Open an invoice to see everything about it.
2. **New invoice** makes an invoice of any amount for an owner''s car, for example a registration fee of $123.45.
3. The monthly run and tracker invoices: **Run the monthly invoices** issues the invoices for the 15th by hand, for a missed month (never twice); **Issue all tracker invoices** bills the Tracker Install for each car waiting for its tracker.

![](/guides/img/admin-14-owner-invoices-desktop-dc4ed1f1.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 1060; address: carmacars.ca/admin/invoices; pins: 1 83.3 22.4, 2 41.7 35.7, 3 29.0 43.4")

## Make, edit and issue an invoice

A new invoice is a draft: the owner sees nothing and it is never debited until you issue it.

1. Choose the car, a title (for example Registration fee) and, if you like, the due date (empty: 7 days after it is issued). Each line: the description, the quantity, the unit amount to the cent, HST on or off, and a note. **Add a line** for more.
2. **Save as draft** to come back to it, or **Save and issue** to send it now. On a draft''s page, **Issue and email** sends it.
3. Paid another way? Press **Record payment** on the invoice. The page lists the payments with their receipts, the automatic debits, the emails sent and the history.
4. **Resend email** sends the invoice again. **PDF** opens it as a PDF.

## Correct an issued invoice

An issued invoice is never edited. You void it and issue a corrected one.

1. Press **Void**, write the reason (the owner reads it), keep Make a corrected invoice from it ticked, and press **Void the invoice**. Its scheduled debit is cancelled and the owner is told.
2. The corrected invoice opens as a draft with the same lines. Fix the amounts and press **Save and issue**.
3. Already paid? Void the payment first, or press **Credit note** for the amount to give back: it gets its own number and the owner sees it.

Invoices issued before October 20, 2026 at the old default (for example $904.00, or $1,017.00 when the Insurance Fee was $450.00) are not changed by themselves. Where an owner agreed another amount, void them and reissue at the agreed amount.

## The automatic debit

The debit runs by itself. Your job is to watch for returned debits and owners without a mandate.

:::flow
Notice day | Invoices issued, one notice per owner, 10 days before
Debit day | The 15th from 6:00: one debit per invoice
Cleared | The invoice is paid
Returned, insufficient funds | The $50.00 Late Fee is added once; the same amount is tried again within 30 days
Returned for another reason | No retry and no Late Fee: the debit pauses and you get a task
:::

1. The tiles show the next debit day and notice day, scheduled, processing, cleared and returned debits.
2. How it runs explains the policy in words, read from Program settings.
3. Scheduled and processing lists each debit. **Pause** holds one (a reason is needed).
4. Owners lists each mandate. Use **Pause**, **Resume** or **Send a notice now**.

![](/guides/img/admin-15-owner-debits-desktop-f65f061a.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 920; address: carmacars.ca/admin/debits; pins: 1 21.8 21.7, 2 21.5 35.5, 3 91.5 75.4, 4 84.7 94.7")

5. Results: each debit, cleared or returned, with the bank''s reason.
6. Run log: each notice and debit run, with its counts.
7. Notices sent: who was told what, for which debit day.

![](/guides/img/admin-15-owner-debits-desktop-8d4682bc.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 520; address: carmacars.ca/admin/debits; pins: 5 11.0 14.4, 6 10.2 52.3, 7 15.4 89.8")

Insufficient funds: the $50.00 Late Fee is added to that invoice once and collected with the owner''s next debit, and the original amount is tried again within 30 days, as section 4.4 of the Enrollment Agreement sets out. The retry is never more than the original amount. Returned again: the invoice is in arrears and you get a task.

> Watch out: Returned for any other reason (account closed, payment stopped, no authorization): there is no retry and no Late Fee. The owner''s debit pauses, the owner gets an email asking them to fix the account or pay another way, and you get a task. A debit is never more than its notice said. An owner with no mandate gets an email on the notice day and you get a task; nothing is debited for them.

## Owner statements

**Money** > **Owner money**, the **Statements** tab

1. Press **Build all for a month** (or **Build one**).
2. Open each draft. Check it, **Rebuild** after a correction, **Preview PDF**, then **Approve**.
3. Press **Issue to the owner**. **Reissue** sends a corrected copy; **CSV** exports it.

![](/guides/img/admin-16-statements-desktop-43a313ea.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 400; address: carmacars.ca/admin/statements; pins: 1 79.9 27.3")

![An approved statement: the owner gets it by email with the PDF on the 10th, and payouts follow under Payouts.](/guides/img/admin-17-statement-desktop-106ee57f.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 520; address: carmacars.ca/admin/statements/2eedf660-50ce-4bd9-86d6-01bbe149c000; pins: 3 86.0 22.7")

## Staff commissions

**Money** > **Company**, the **Commissions** tab. Nothing is paid automatically.

:::flow
Not earned yet | The rental is ahead, or not paid in full
Pending approval | Completed and paid in full; a Sales month once it has ended
Approved | You approved it; the staff member is told
Paid | You recorded the payment; the staff member is told
Reversed | Cancelled, refunded or charged back; after payment it comes off the next payment
:::

1. By person shows each staff member''s month (Sales: rental days of 100 and the tier), what is not earned yet, pending approval, approved and paid.
2. Press **Approve** on a person (everything that may be approved now) or on one commission.
3. Press **Record a payment**: choose how it was paid (e-Transfer, bank transfer, Wise, cash, the monthly pay statement or another way), the reference and the date.
4. **Prices to review** lists prices typed by hand; **Sourcing claims** lists staff who say they sourced a website request; **Payments made** lists each payment.
5. **Owner requests** lists the commission each salesperson asks for an owner they brought in: a flat amount, or a percent of the company''s share or of the cars'' rental revenue, for a number of months or for as long as the car is with us. Press **Approve**, **Change and approve** (your terms, with a note) or **Decline**. Nothing accrues before you approve. A flat amount is earned at the owner''s first paid rental, once; a percent on each paid rental of the owner''s cars in the time approved. Each then comes to the list above for approval.
6. Who sourced an owner: the owner''s page, **Sourced by**. Only an Admin changes it, with a reason. A waiting request of the person before is withdrawn; an approved one, with what it has not paid yet, goes to the new person.

|  | Commission |
| --- | --- |
| Sales | By rental days of the month: under 50 days 10%, from 50 days 15%, from 100 days 20%, on all that month''s rentals |
| An owner a salesperson brought in | The request you approved. A CarmaCars expense, never deducted before Owner Revenue; none on CarmaCars'', a partner''s or a shareholder''s cars |
| Customer service, finance, fleet, field staff | 10% (also the field referral fee) |
| Base | The rental charge before tax, after discounts, with late extra days; never delivery, kilometres, add-ons or anything else bought. Only a refund of the rental charge comes off |
| On the owner statement | An owner''s car: deducted with the kickbacks before Owner Revenue, its own line on the statement. A partner''s car: from CarmaCars'' commission. A CarmaCars-owned car: a CarmaCars expense |

> Tip: A commission that changes after an owner statement was built (a refund, or the month''s Sales tier) goes on the owner''s next statement as an adjustment line.

## Field pay

**Money** > **Company**, the **Field pay** tab. Field staff clock in and out on their phones (My hours); you run the pay every two weeks. Nothing is paid automatically.

:::flow
Clocked in and out | Field staff press Clock in and Clock out; Fleet or you fix a forgotten clock-out
Pay run started | Hours times the hourly rate, plus the approved commissions
Approved | The figures are frozen, the period''s hours are locked, the statements are numbered
Paid | You recorded how each person was paid; they get their statement by email
:::

1. The tab **Pay run** shows the current two-week period (Sunday to Saturday: the first day is Settings > Program, Field pay). **Earlier period** and **Later period** move between periods.
2. After the period ends, press **Start the pay run**: one line for each person with hours times their hourly rate, plus the staff commissions and referral fees approved by the end of the period (see Staff commissions). **Refresh the figures** takes in a change made since.
3. Press **Approve**. The period''s hours are locked, each line gets a statement number and the figures are frozen. Someone still clocked in blocks it: fix their shift under **Hours** first. **Withdraw** takes an approved run back while no payment is recorded.
4. Press **Record payment** on a line: choose e-Transfer, bank transfer or cash, the reference (not needed for cash) and the date. The commissions in the line are marked paid and the person gets their pay statement by email (**Send again** repeats it). The statement''s number opens its PDF; **CSV** gives the run for your accountant.
5. **Hours** lists everyone''s shifts of the period. **Add hours** enters a shift for someone who forgot to clock in, **Change** fixes one and **Remove** takes one out. Each needs a reason and is kept in a log. Fleet does the same under Field hours but sees no pay.
6. **Hourly rates** shows each person''s rate: CA$18.00 an hour unless you give them their own with **Set the rate** (a reason is needed). A pay run keeps the rate it was started with.

|  | Field pay |
| --- | --- |
| Overtime | Off. Settings > Program, Field pay: pay overtime, after 44 hours in a week, at 150% of the rate |
| Vacation pay | Off. Settings > Program, Field pay: vacation pay (Ontario: 4%) adds that share of wages, overtime and commissions to each statement |
| Deductions | None are worked out: income tax, CPP, EI and the employer''s contributions are for your accountant. Each statement says so |
| Commissions that net to nothing | A person whose approved commissions add up to nothing or less (a clawback) is not paid them this period: they carry to the next |

> Tip: A shift of more than 16 hours (a setting) is refused, and so are hours that overlap another shift of the same person. The field staff member sees their hours and statements under My hours on their phone.

## Company model

Money > **Company model** is the CarmaCars model workbook, live: the actuals, the forecast and the pro forma on one page. Admins only (not Finance). Never share it: investors have their own sheets in the investor portal.

1. **Forecast**: the latest actual month, the EBITDA break-even month, the next 12 months'' EBITDA and the lowest cash, a chart of EBITDA and cash, and 36 months marked A (actual) or F (forecast): cars, utilization, revenue per rented day, revenue, costs, EBITDA, investor returns, tax and cash.
2. **Actuals**: filled in by themselves every hour from the bookings, payments, payouts, expenses and investments. Rental earned is spread over each rental''s days (before HST, insurer-billed and renter-billed apart, placeholders left out), with fees by kind, cash received by method, rentals and rented days, owner and partner shares, commissions, kickbacks, expenses by category and investor payouts. **Refresh actuals now** recomputes them at once.
3. **Pro forma 5 years**: each year''s income statement, cash flow and key figures.
4. **Assumptions**: growth, the utilization ramp, rates, monthly costs, hires, planned capital raises, the fleet insurance premium and tax. Press **Save the assumptions**; the forecast, the pro forma and the download use them at once. A field marked "From the actuals" left blank uses the latest complete month.
5. **Download as Excel**: the full internal workbook with live formulas and the current actuals.

> Tip: Enter the fleet insurance premium under Assumptions; until then it counts as $0 and profit is overstated. Enter each month''s costs in Money > Expenses: a cost line with nothing entered for an actual month uses the assumption, marked est.

## Company statements

**Money** > **Company**, the **Monthly statements** tab: CarmaCars'' own monthly statement, in twelve sections.

1. Choose the month. The tiles show revenue, fees, refunds, expenses and the company net.
2. Switch between Total, Per owner and Per vehicle.
3. Download **PDF**, **PDF by owner** or **PDF by vehicle**, or press **Email me the PDFs**.
4. **Finalize** freezes the month. **Rebuild** works until then.

![](/guides/img/admin-18-company-statements-desktop-8e2738ed.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 760; address: carmacars.ca/admin/reports; pins: 1 20.8 28.0, 2 19.4 59.3, 3 77.1 15.5, 4 46.9 15.5")

### Fees taken from the revenue statement
On an owner''s page, the **Fees** button sets **How fees are paid**: **Bank debit** (the default) or **Take from revenue statement**. Taken from the statement, the owner''s invoices (not the upfront one) are not debited: the next owner statement pays each one from the payout, as far as it goes, with the line "Invoice INV-..., paid from statement". Approved, the invoice reads **Paid from statement**, or part paid with the rest on the next statement. An invoice still owing 2 months after its billing date goes back to the bank debit after the usual notice, and you get the task **Invoice ... back to the bank debit**.

### The flat-rate agreements
An owner whose every car is on a flat monthly payment signs the **Flat-Rate Vehicle Enrollment Agreement** instead of the standard one (the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement and Forms A to D are the same). The owner''s page says which set applies. When the pay model changes, the signed Enrollment Agreement ends and the owner signs the new one in the owner portal; changed back before signing, the signed one is in force again. The lawyer approved the flat-rate set: Program settings > **Flat-rate agreements awaiting lawyer OK** is off, and is turned on only to mark a new text still under review. Owners can sign either way.

## How it''s paid: bank debit or deducted from payouts

Every owner invoice is paid one of two ways: **Bank debit on the 15th**, or **Deduct from payouts** (taken from the owner''s monthly payouts until paid, never debited).

1. On an invoice, **How it''s paid**, **Change**. A draft changed to Deduct from payouts is issued without the debit email.
2. Each monthly statement deducts as much as the payout allows and shows it to the owner as a deduction; the rest waits for the next statement. The invoice screen shows what was deducted and what is left.
3. For the first and last month, choose **Deduct from payouts** on the Terms tab (or at approval).
4. On the Terms tab, **Charge the agreed one-off fees** makes one invoice for a car from the one-off fees agreed on the owner''s terms (all, or the ones you name), deducted from payouts or debited.

## Referral links between owners (release 28)

When one owner referred another, open the referrer''s **Terms** tab, **Referral links**, **This owner referred another owner**: choose the owner referred and the share in basis points (1000 = 10 points of the revenue the management fee is taken from). Set the referred owner''s own fee on their Terms as usual (for example a 40% management fee and $350 a month per car). Every statement of the referrer then has a **Referral share** line per referred car; it is paid from CarmaCars'' share, never the referred owner''s payout. With **sees the cars** on, the referrer finds **Cars you referred** in their owner portal: bookings, use and revenue, read only, without the other owner''s details. **End** stops the link; shares already earned are still paid.', 'Owner money', 'Owner invoices (drafts, void and reissue, credit notes), the automatic debit, statements, payouts and the company statement.',
  'Owner fee invoices are issued on the notice day and debited on the 15th. Invoices of any amount are made by hand, as drafts first. Statements are built, approved and issued each month, and payouts follow.

## Owner invoices

**Money** > **Owner money**, the **Invoices** tab. Every owner invoice, drafts and voids included. The same list is on each owner''s and each application''s Invoices tab.

1. Filter by Drafts, Open, Partly paid, Paid, Failed, In arrears or Void, or search by invoice number or owner. Open an invoice to see everything about it.
2. **New invoice** makes an invoice of any amount for an owner''s car, for example a registration fee of $123.45.
3. The monthly run and tracker invoices: **Run the monthly invoices** issues the invoices for the 15th by hand, for a missed month (never twice); **Issue all tracker invoices** bills the Tracker Install for each car waiting for its tracker.

![](/guides/img/admin-14-owner-invoices-desktop-dc4ed1f1.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 1060; address: carmacars.ca/admin/invoices; pins: 1 83.3 22.4, 2 41.7 35.7, 3 29.0 43.4")

## Make, edit and issue an invoice

